## Abstract

We identify a single object underneath the information-geometric mechanics of
Papers 13–31 and show that it answers, rather than merely guards, the questions
the series has been circling: the cumulant tower of the categorical
log-partition \(\Phi=\log Z\) is a categorical effective action, whose four
successive covariant derivatives are the objects ordinary physics names
separately only because it presupposes a manifold — position, the Fisher metric
*as simultaneously space and inertia*, the Amari–Chentsov force, and the
time-translation closure defect — yielding the exact identities *space and mass
are the same (second) cumulant* and *time, energy, and gravity are the
time-translation Noether generator and the obstruction to integrating it
globally*. We make this computational by proving the explicit five-slot
projection-closure certificate (Paper 31, Def. 5.1) for the time-translation
projection on \(R=\mathbb{Z}/6\mathbb{Z}\): from the exact cubic structure
constant \(T_{klm}=216\cdot\mathbb{1}[k{+}l{+}m\equiv0\bmod6]\) (a Pontryagin
identity, basis-independent and stable to all centroid orders) the certificate
is closure-valid *exactly* on the single-prime block \(A_2\oplus A_3\) —
re-deriving Paper 17's Cartan \(\mathfrak{u}(1)^2\) exhaustion from projection
closure rather than representation theory — while its entire typed, bounded,
recurrent residual is provably supported on the conductor-6 carry, coinciding
with \(\operatorname{Ext}_{CH}\) (Paper 13), the simplex-mass jerk (Paper 20),
and the dark-matter-adjacent residual Paper 28 §13 could only name, with
non-tachyonicity *identical* to Paper 22's primorial Noether–Weil positivity at
the \(P_2=2\cdot3\) row. From this we obtain a **dimensional selection
principle**: an inertial projector (one Hamiltonian, one energy, one rotation
axis, one \(J^2{=}{-}I\)) admits a closure-valid self-model in *exactly one*
row of the Fisher-volume hierarchy, \(Q=4\), spatial dimension three — by two
independent routes (the \(\mathfrak{so}(n)\)/Hodge uniqueness at \(n=3\), now
anchored to the Zhang–Li properness condition, and the \(1+2\) conductor count)
— so experiencing space as three-dimensional is the closure certificate of
*having mass*, with the complementary conductor-6 packet not perceived as space
but as the gravity-adjacent residual: the two findings are one finding. Each
[P] result is anchored to peer-reviewed external precedent (Zhang–Li
divergence-symplectic geometry; the Koszul–Souriau–Fisher capacity identity;
the Souriau symplectic-cohomology cocycle) without adopting the
emergent-gravity ontology this paper explicitly positions against. **Gravity is
not claimed; the form of gravity, its arithmetic localization, and the
selection of spatial dimension three are.**

> **Conditional statement (claimable after the three audits of §13).**
> Subject to (i) the depth audit (§13.1): the conductor-6 residual stays on the
> squarefree mode, bounded and sign-definite, under
> \(\mathbb{Z}/6\hookrightarrow\mathbb{Z}/12,\mathbb{Z}/18\); (ii) the
> Souriau-cocycle audit (§13.3): the time-translation non-equivariance defect
> is a nontrivial cocycle class supported on conductor 6; and (iii) the
> Bures-dispersion audit (§13.2): on the lifted conductor-2 ⊕ conductor-3 block
> the level set \(\operatorname{tr}(H\rho)=E\) is a genuine two-sheeted
> hyperboloid invariant under a 3-parameter Cartan-completing group — then
> additionally: *gravity-as-Noether-anomaly is a named Souriau cocycle class*,
> and *Lorentzian \(3+1\), nonabelian gauge restoration, the imaginary leakage
> energy, and the existence of a finite frame-independent invariant speed
> (\(c\equiv1\) in internal units, the energy–momentum hyperboloid's asymptote
> — "the time-translation limit of mass") are one and the same Bures-lift
> event* (one lift, four faces; Corollary 9.7), the classical real-simplex
> level being only Galilean (parabolic dispersion — hence no causal speed
> limit — forced by the Poincaré–Cartan \(-\ell_3\) sign). Should (iii) instead
> return a definite level set, the equally claimed alternative is that the
> framework is *intrinsically Euclidean-4* with no invariant speed. Both
> branches are pre-claimed (§12, items K, L, J′); neither is asserted here. The
> value of \(c\) in any physical unit is never claimed (§11.2 firewall). This
> conditional is stated in the manner of Paper 22's RH program: a proved
> formal implication plus three named finite inputs, not an unconditional
> claim.

> **Spine sentence — the minimal independent face count (Corollary 9.8 /
> §12 item V′; claimable after S′ ∧ T′ ∧ U′; Corollary 9.7 preserved
> layered as the assertable-today statement).**  *Counting what S′, T′
> and U′ leave of "one lift, four faces": one Bures lift produces three
> forced internal faces — Face A (the ℂ²-leg algebraic real-form face,
> carrying weak-\(\mathrm{SU}(2)\) as its compact form and
> Lorentz/(3+1)/the invariant \(c\) as its non-compact form, the latter
