## 1. Scope and Claim Status

This paper consolidates the series into one statement and discharges, in part,
the guardrail of Paper 31 §13 ("projection-closure theory explains the *form*
of the gravity question, not gravity itself"). The discharge is partial and
explicitly typed. We use a three-tier status convention throughout.

- **[P] Proven here, unconditionally**, given Papers 13 and 17 as cited.
- **[A] Structural, pending a named finite audit.** The argument is complete;
  one specified finite computation converts it to [P] or refutes it.
- **[C] Conjectural, reduced.** Stated with an explicit falsifier and a single
  runnable verification; not asserted as true, asserted as *seen and reduced*.

### 1.1 Claims kept on the table

1. **[P]** \(\Phi=\log Z\) is a categorical effective action; its first four
   cumulant-tower derivatives are position, the Fisher metric (= space =
   inertia), the Amari–Chentsov force, and the time-translation closure defect.
2. **[P]** *Space and mass are the same tensor* (second cumulant). *Time,
   energy, gravity share the time-translation Noether structure and its
   closure failure.*
3. **[P]** The explicit five-slot time-translation closure certificate on
   \(R=\mathbb{Z}/6\mathbb{Z}\): closure-valid exactly on \(A_2\oplus A_3\);
   typed bounded recurrent residual localized to the conductor-6 packet \(M\).
   The selection rule is proved exactly (Lemma 6.1a: the cubic structure
   constant is \(216\cdot\mathbb{1}[k{+}l{+}m\equiv0\bmod 6]\) by Pontryagin
   duality), basis-independently (6.1b), and stably to all centroid orders
   (6.1c); the packet partition is the exhaustive six-multiset enumeration
   (Lemma 6.1) with three exact consequences (Corollary 6.1d).
4. **[P]** This re-derives Paper 17 Cartan \(\mathfrak{u}(1)^2\) exhaustion
   from projection closure, independently of representation theory.
5. **[P]** The conductor-6 residual coincides with \(\operatorname{Ext}_{CH}\)
   (Paper 13 §11), the simplex-mass jerk (Paper 20), and Paper 28 §13's
   dark-matter-adjacent residual; its non-tachyonicity is the cubic-order
   instance of Paper 22's Weil positivity.
6. **[P]** Dimensional selection: an inertial projector closes in exactly one
   row, \(Q=4\), spatial dimension three. Two independent derivations agree.
7. **[P]** Classical signature \((3,1)\) from the Poincaré–Cartan \(-\ell_3\)
   sign, but Galilean (parabolic dispersion); no classical Lorentz structure,
   consistent with the series.
8. **[A]** Residual stays on the squarefree conductor-6 mode and sign-definite
   under prime-power depth — pending the
   \(\mathbb{Z}/6\hookrightarrow\mathbb{Z}/12,\mathbb{Z}/18\) audit (§13.1).
9. **[C]** Lorentzian \(3+1\) is a Bures-lift phenomenon, unified with gauge
   restoration and the imaginary energy — reduced to the Bures-dispersion
   audit (§13.2). The Euclidean-4 alternative is itself a stated result.
10. **[A, conditional on S′ ∧ T′ ∧ U′; Cor 9.7 preserved]** *The minimal
    independent face count* (Corollary 9.8 / §12 item V′). Counting what
    S′, T′ and U′ leave of "one lift, four faces": **three forced
    internal faces** (Face A = ℂ²-leg algebraic real-form face carrying
    \(\mathrm{SU}(2)\) compact + Lorentz/(3+1)/\(c\) non-compact at the
    algebraic + §13.2A local-tangent levels; Face B = ℂ³-leg color; Face
    C = \(i\)-face carrying the \(\hbar\)-role), **one carried datum**
    of open face/mode status (the inter-leg central \(\mathfrak u(1)\),
    Paper 18 Prop 5.1), **one external bit** (chirality
    \(\mathbb Z_2\) locked to \(\gamma^5\), Paper 33 §3), and **one
    constants clause** (U′: only conductor-fixed pure numbers; Compton
    wavelength named as the firewall trap; target 1 already settled-
    negative). A stated degradation ladder forces every failure path to
    a weaker stated count, never to silence.

### 1.2 Terminology

We keep "cubic" for third-cumulant order and "row" for a fixed modulus \(R\),
following Papers 13–28. "Inertial projector" is new and defined in §8.
"Closure-valid" and the certificate tuple are Paper 31. "Lift" always means
the Bures density-matrix completion of Paper 18.

