## 5. Time, Energy, Gravity Share One Structure

Paper 17 Theorem 2.2: time-translation invariance of the autonomous cubic
action yields the conserved Noether energy
\[
\mathcal E_3=\dot\eta\cdot\frac{\partial\ell_3}{\partial\dot\eta}-\ell_3
=\tfrac12 g(\dot\eta,\dot\eta)+\tfrac13 T(h,\dot\eta,\dot\eta),
\qquad \tfrac{d}{dt}\mathcal E_3=0 \text{ on stationary cubic paths.}
\]
Paper 20: on the *projected* back-path \(\mathcal E_3\) is no longer autonomous
and the jerk \(\nabla^{(e)}T=T^{(4)}\) reappears as the curvature of the
projected energy bookkeeping.

**Theorem 5.1 (Noether-anomaly view of gravity). [P]**
Time, energy, and gravity share one structure: the time-translation generator
and the obstruction to integrating it globally. Energy is its *local* conserved
current. The gravity-adjacent stress is its *global holonomy* under a
non-closing projection — the typed residual that appears precisely because the
real simplex cannot classically carry the nonabelian directions the
third-order response demands (Papers 14, 17), so the projected shadow pays a
curvature cost to remain on the real-positive cone. Integrated, that cost is
gravity-adjacent.

This is the precise sense in which "what do time, energy, and gravity have in
common" has a one-line answer: energy is the Noether current of time
translation; gravity is the curvature that makes that current fail to be
globally conserved unless the geometry absorbs the deficit — structurally the
same role \(\nabla\!\cdot T=0\) plays as the Bianchi integrability condition of
general relativity, here realized as the fundamental/Filippov identity of the
\((Q-1)\)-ary Nambu–Fisher bracket and its controlled failure.

**Remark 5.2 (The residual is a categorical Souriau cocycle class).
[A, named external object]**
Souriau's Lie-group thermodynamics already names the obstruction to a moment
map being globally equivariant: the symplectic-cohomology *cocycle*
\(\theta(g)\), which corrects the transport of the heat moment under the
adjoint action, \(Q(\mathrm{Ad}(g)\beta)=\mathrm{Ad}^*(g)Q(\beta)+\theta(g)\),
when the dynamic group has non-null cohomology. This is exactly the structure
of Theorem 5.1: the gravity-adjacent residual is the failure of the
time-translation moment to be equivariant under the projection \(\Pi_\tau\).
We therefore type the residual not merely as an internal carry but as **the
categorical realization of a nontrivial Souriau cocycle class** of the
time-translation projection. This is stated as [A]: §13.3 specifies the finite
computation of that cocycle class on \(R=\mathbb{Z}/6\mathbb{Z}\) and the
prediction that it is supported on the conductor-6 packet, converting "gravity
= Noether anomaly" from an internal slogan into a cocycle-class statement with
an established external name and an explicit test.

**Remark 5.2A (One projection non-closure, two ledger readings — magnitude
to gravity, sign to the arrow).**  Theorem 5.1's projection non-closure
has two distinct readings of the *same* object: its **magnitude** is the
gravity-adjacent stress (the LHS of the Einstein-like equation, §9.7
Corollary 9.10; ledger item R′), and its **sign** is the arrow of time
(§9.6 Corollary 9.9; ledger item W′). One non-closure, two ledger items
— magnitude → R′, sign → W′ — unified under one object. They share the
same Face A local-Casimir host, the same Face C \(\hbar\)-clock, the
same U′ firewall on what is and is not inferable, and the same Paper 18
§6 Petz–Bures monotonicity node (no new audit for the structural half
of either). The same \(m^2_{\text{simplex}}\ge 0\) inequality (Paper 20
Rmk 2.2) underwrites both: it is the weak-energy/no-tachyon condition
on the R′ side and the monotonicity of the W′ arrow on the W′ side.
This is a bookkeeping unification, not a new derivation. **Three
readings, not two (§9.10 Corollary 9.12 / item Z′).** The same
projection non-closure now has a *third* reading — *the non-negativity
of its magnitude*, \(m^2_{\text{simplex}}\ge 0\), is the Raychaudhuri
focusing-term non-negativity \(R_{ab}u^au^b\ge 0\) (the energy
condition that powers the singularity-theorem focusing linkage). One
object, three readings: sign = arrow (W′), magnitude = Einstein-like
source (R′), non-negativity of the magnitude = energy condition /
Raychaudhuri focusing scalar (Z′). The shear–rotation tensor sector
is owned *not at all, by construction*: the program has a projection
channel, not a spacetime congruence (§11.1 boundary, do-not-cut).

### 5.A The general-relativistic triad, made explicit

Theorem 5.1's "Noether-anomaly view of gravity" is the program's first
arrival at a GR-shaped object. The slogan that "gravity is curvature"
understates what GR actually is, and obscures which parts of GR the program is
already entitled to and which remain conjectural; we tabulate this here. GR is
not a single statement but a *nested triad*: (i) a uniqueness principle that
fixes the metric structure with no prior geometry, (ii) the assertion that
free trajectories are its geodesics, and (iii) the identification of the
gravitational force with the connection's deviation from a flat comparison.
The categorical program realizes all three, and its first member is *stronger*
than Einstein's.

| GR object | Program homolog | Tier |
|---|---|---|
| general covariance (postulate) | Chentsov / Petz–Sudár monotone-metric uniqueness + SLD/Bures selection (Paper 18 §6) | **[P]-spirit**, Paper 18 §6 finite check |
| metric \(g_{\mu\nu}\) | Fisher / Bures second cumulant \(g=\nabla^{(2)}\Phi\) (§4 Thm 4.1) | **[P]** |
| Levi-Civita selection | SLD/Bures selection in the Petz–Sudár monotone family (Paper 18 Thm 6.1) | **[A]** |
| connection / gravitational field | Amari–Chentsov cubic tensor \(T\) (the \(\alpha\)-connection gap) | **[P/A]** |
| geodesic / free fall | cubic force law \(\ddot\eta=T(v,v)\) (Paper 17 / §5) | **[P]** |
| stress–energy source | projection-closure residual / jerk \(T^{(4)}\) (Paper 20) | **[P]** |
| weak-energy / no-tachyon condition | \(m^2_{\text{simplex}}\ge0\) (Paper 20 Rmk 2.2) | **[P]** |
| Bianchi \(\nabla\!\cdot T=0\) | Filippov/fundamental identity of the Nambu–Fisher bracket (Thm 5.1) | **[P]** |

The single sentence not to lose is the asymmetry on the first row: **the
program's "general covariance" is a uniqueness theorem (Chentsov for the
classical Fisher metric; Petz–Sudár with the SLD/Bures selection for the lift,
Paper 18 Theorem 6.1) — where General Relativity's is a postulate.** The
Levi-Civita selection out of all metric-compatible connections has its program
analog in the SLD/Bures selection out of all monotone information-geometric
metrics; the same Paper 18 §6 finite Petz–Bures check discharges both. The
gravitational *field strength* is the third cumulant: \(T\) is precisely the
gap between the Levi-Civita (\(\alpha=0\)) connection and the
exponential/mixture (\(\alpha=\pm 1\)) connections, and \(T(v,v)\) is the cubic
force — geometric, not substantial, with no added primitive.

**Remark 5.3 (Scope: fixed constant-curvature background, not Einstein
gravity).** What the program owns today is a *fixed* constant-curvature
geometry. The Fisher metric on \(\Delta_R^\circ\), pulled back through the
square-root/Hellinger embedding (Paper 13 Definition 14.6A, Remark 14.6A.1),
is a sector of a round sphere of radius \(2\) — constant positive curvature in
Riemannian signature, *not* Einsteinian. There is no back-reaction of the
matter content on \(g\) at this level. The conjectural promotion to a *sourced*
curvature — the Einstein-like equation
\(\delta\mathcal R_{\text{proj}}\propto T^{(4)}\) — is opened as ledger item R′
(§12), tied to Paper 20 OQ1/OQ2 as its dynamical entry points. The matched-pair
branch (the projected curvature defect is rigidly independent of \(T^{(4)}\),
capping the homolog at fixed-background permanently) is itself a stated
result, pre-claimed alongside the positive branch. The dimensional firewall
(§11.2) is binding here: the GR homolog is a *structural* prediction (the
relation form), never a dimensionful curvature magnitude — no Newton constant,
no length scale, no \(G\). Even if R′ confirms, the program does not derive
General Relativity, Newton's constant, spacetime, or a physical field equation;
what is owned is the projection-closure *form* of why a GR-shaped structure is
constrained on the simplex. The heaviest §11.1 emergent-gravity positioning
applies here.

### 5.B T14 promotion: cubic vertex IS projected curvature (gravity-as-closure-defect, geometric form) [P, proved geometric — added v0.2.5; ledger YY]

The §5 / §5.A reading — *gravity = projection-closure defect; cubic vertex = Amari–Chentsov tensor = the geometric face of the closure defect* — acquires a precise geometric statement under T14 (Murillo Montero 2026, "Projected Flatness and Curvature Linearization").

**T14 Theorem 2 (Curvature as Projection-Commutator).** For a flat lifted connection $\nabla$ on the apex / ledger algebra and a smooth projection $\Pi$ onto a retained sector, the curvature of the projected connection $\nabla^\Pi=\Pi\nabla$ is
\[
R^\Pi(X,Y)=\Pi\big((\nabla_X\Pi)(\nabla_Y\Pi)-(\nabla_Y\Pi)(\nabla_X\Pi)\big)=\Pi\,d\Pi\wedge d\Pi\,\Pi.
\]
Curvature is the obstruction to projection commuting with flat lifted transport.

**T14 Theorem 3 (Boundary Curvature).** For conductor-packet projections $\Pi_S$, the universal support of the projected curvature defect
\[
\mathcal R_S^{(n)}=(1-\Pi_S-\Pi_1)V_n\big|_{H_S^{\otimes n}}
\]
is **exactly the conductor-fusion boundary** $\partial_n S=\operatorname{Fuse}_n(S)\setminus(S\cup\{1\})$. The support is sharp: every packet in $\partial_n S$ is attained by some retained character inputs.

**Instance at Paper 32 §6.4.** $N=6$, $n=3$, $S=\{2,3\}$, $\partial_3\{2,3\}=\{6\}$:
\[
\mathcal R_{\{2,3\}}^{(3)}(H_S,H_S,H_S)\subseteq H_6=M.
\]
**The gravity-adjacent residual of Paper 32 Theorem 6.2 IS the projected cubic curvature defect of $V=A_2\oplus A_3$, supported on the M-packet, sharply.** §10.6.7n (item VV) gives the explicit channel-level basis: the two cubic boundary-source channels $\{3,2,2\}\to\chi_1$ and $\{3,4,4\}\to\chi_5$ are *also* the explicit basis of $\mathcal R_{\{2,3\}}^{(3)}$.

**T14 Theorem 6 (Equivalence, capstone).** In the finite apex setting,
\[
\boxed{
\text{curvature}=\text{projection noncommutation}=\text{boundary leakage}=\text{renormalization source}=\text{Noether defect}=\text{beta source}.
}
\]
Paper 32's "closure defect / cubic vertex / gravity-adjacent residual / RG-source" cluster is **one finite object** in six languages. The §5 reading "cubic vertex = Amari–Chentsov = the projection-closure defect" is now one face of T14 Theorem 6.

**Tier upgrade.** §5 / §5.A gravity-as-closure-defect reading: [A, structural] / [P, structural] → **[P, proved geometric]** via T14 Thm 2 + Thm 3 + Thm 6.

**What the firewall still blocks.** The tier upgrade is *structural-geometric*, not dimensionful. T14 does **not** supply Newton's constant, Planck curvature, Ricci-scalar magnitudes in $\mathrm{km}^{-2}$, or any other dimensionful curvature scale. By §11.2.2 / item WW (the Firewall Theorem), the projected curvature defect lives on the finite combinatorial lattice $\mathcal D_N$ and therefore carries no physical-unit content. The promotion is to "[P, proved geometric, dimensionless]," consistent with the C4 strengthening of the firewall theorem (§11.2.2). Item R′ (§9.7 Corollary 9.10, the Einstein-like sourcing conjecture) remains [C, reduced]; T14 does not advance it.

Recorded as **ledger item YY** in §12, paired with **ledger item XX** (T14 substrate).

