## 7. The Positivity Identification

**Theorem 7.1 (Mass non-tachyonicity = Weil positivity at cubic order). [P]**
Paper 20 requires the simplex mass term to be non-tachyonic ("the jerk is
always non-negative"). Paper 22's route is: the all-order Noether energy on the
primorial critical leaf converges to the Weil explicit-formula quadratic form,
and Weil positivity \(\iff\) RH. On \(R=\mathbb{Z}/6\mathbb{Z}=P_2\) these are
not two facts. The conductor-6 residual energy of Theorem 6.2 is the cubic-order
instance of the primorial Noether form. Its sign-definiteness is the
cubic-order instance of Weil positivity. Hence the stability slot
\(\mathsf S^{\Pi_\tau}_W\) of the gravity-adjacent residual *is* Paper 22's
positivity condition evaluated at this row and order.

**Consequence.** The stability of the would-be gravity sector and the Riemann
Hypothesis are, in this architecture, the *same boundedness-below requirement*
at cubic order versus the all-order limit. The energy spectrum of the effective
geometry is indexed by conductor packets (primes); the would-be "graviton
spectrum" is arithmetic. This is recorded as a [P] structural identification at
the \(P_2\) row and a [C] conjecture at the all-order limit (the latter is
exactly Paper 22's open program; we add only the gravity-sector reading).

**RH-bridge status pin (do-not-cut; against downstream compression).**
The \(P_2\)/cubic identification of this theorem is the **exact
base-case shadow** (Paper 22 §9.2) of the **all-order Primorial
Noether–Weil Identity** (Paper 22 Conjecture 5.2: the all-order limit
\(\mathcal Q_n(\mathscr R_n f)\to\mathcal W_\zeta(f*f^*)\), of which
Paper 22 §5.2 states verbatim "this is the whole game — if Conjecture
5.2 is proved, the Riemann Hypothesis follows"). The all-order limit
is **[C]**, cornered by Paper 22 §8 into four named classical
obligations (Lemma 8.1 — primorial-smooth von Mangoldt recovery, the
TOP TASK; double-cutoff commutation; primorial uniformity; the
archimedean Noether limit, Thm 5.2.2), **none discharged**. The
admissible statement, fixed here so no future redraft can compress
past it: *Paper 32 §7's positivity identification is [P] at the
\(P_2\) cubic row and [C] at the all-order limit; the all-order limit
is Paper 22 Conjecture 5.2, cornered into four named classical
obligations, none discharged.* The shadow is real; it is the shadow
of base camp, not the summit. Any compression of "the cubic match is
exact" into "the RH bridge is established" is the Paper 22 §11
"Unsafe statement" and is a guardrail violation — cut, do not edit.

