### 9.6 Causal structure and the arrow of time as the projection-channel dual of the lift

**Corollary 9.9 (Causal structure and the arrow of time as the
projection-channel dual of the lift) [A]/[C], strength-graded per §1.5
below; \([P]\) at its robust core].** *The single Bures lift and its
diagonal/measurement projection are one monotone-metric structure read
in two directions. The very theorem that forces the metric (Chentsov /
Petz–Sudár / Paper 18 §6 uniqueness — the program's
general-covariance analog) also forces the arrow (the same metric's
contraction under the projection is the data-processing inequality,
hence an H-theorem). The lift adds the faces of §9 going up; the
projection is their arrow-bearing dual coming down.*

**Robust core (\([P]\)) — the \(m^2\ge0\) triple unification.**  The
single inequality \(m^2_{\text{simplex}}(\mathbf C)\ge 0\) of Paper 20
Remark 2.2 is simultaneously:

1. the program's **weak-energy / no-tachyon condition** (the
   gravity-homolog dictionary entry; the LHS sign condition for item
   R′);
2. the **monotonicity of the arrow** — the decay exponent of
   \(P_{\text{survive}}(t)\sim\exp(-c(\mathbf C)\,m^2_{\text{simplex}}\,t)\)
   is sign-definite, so the channel loss has a fixed direction (no
   spontaneous distinguishability gain);
3. the **second law in program form** — the projected dynamics cannot
   un-mix.

Three physical statements, one proven inequality. This is the robust
core and is unaffected by every degradation path below.

**The causal trichotomy on Face A's local-Casimir hyperboloid.**  The
projection-closure residual — the jerk \(T^{(4)}\) of Paper 20 — has a
sign that partitions tangent directions; the partition is read on
**Face A's hyperboloid in the §13.2A local-tangent Casimir-Hessian
sense** (the manifold-level mass-shell was refuted by §13.2, so the
trichotomy lives only at the local-tangent layer where Face A actually
realizes Lorentzian \((1,3)\) signature):

| Causal class | Residual condition | Program sector | Face A reading (local-tangent) |
|---|---|---|---|
| **spacelike-candidate** | **zero** projection-closure residual | the Cartan / real-cone-internal sector — classically closed, on-cone, reversible-looking, conserved-energy directions (Paper 14 Thm 2.2′; Paper 20 centroid \(m^2=0\)) | no preferred time direction |
| **timelike-candidate** | **positive** residual | the leakage-paying sector — nonabelian directions forced back through the diagonal channel, steadily losing conductor mass (Paper 20 §3) | has a definite time-orientation (the decay direction) |
| **null** | **exactly-vanishing** residual (the *boundary*, not the interior zero) | the leakage-balance locus | the cone itself = the local-Casimir asymptote where \(c\) is read (§9.3 Part 2 / §13.2A) |

**The arrow proper, and why it is a projection phenomenon.**  Upstairs
the conservative Nambu–Bures flow is unitary von Neumann evolution
(Paper 18 §4); the jerk *vanishes* there — unitary flow is reversible,
no arrow. The arrow appears **only** in the projected channel, because
the diagonal embedding / measurement channel is non-invertible and the
Bures metric is non-increasing under it (Petz monotonicity, Paper 18
§6). The non-invertible loss of distinguishability *is* time's arrow;
its existence is the exact dual of the lift adding distinguishability
structure going up.

**The speed-limit/arrow split (one metric, two roles).**  The
Mandelstam–Tamm/Bures relation (Face C's \(\hbar\)-role, T′) bounds the
Bures distinguishability rate *above* by the energy spread — that
ceiling is the local-Casimir asymptote slope, the invariant \(c\)
(Face A, §9.3 Part 2 + §13.2A). The *same* metric's contraction signs
the rate's *direction* (the arrow). **One metric: its
Mandelstam–Tamm bound caps the rate's magnitude (the speed limit
\(c\)); its monotone contraction signs the rate's direction (the
arrow / second law).** Read in Face C's \(\hbar\)-units, under U′'s
firewall on what is and is not inferable.

**Two structural ties.**

- *To §5 Theorem 5.1 (Noether-anomaly view of gravity).*  The same
  projection non-closure whose **magnitude** is gravity-adjacent
  (Theorem 5.1; ledger item R′, the Einstein-like equation entry) has
  a **sign** that is the arrow (Corollary 9.9; ledger item W′). One
  projection non-closure, two readings — its magnitude is the
  gravity homolog's source, its sign is the arrow of time.
- *To Paper 33 §3 (Chirality Boundary; orientation bookkeeping
  splits).*  **Time-orientation (the arrow) is internal** — it is the
  projection channel's monotonicity, this corollary. **Chirality
  \(\mathbb Z_2\) (\(\gamma^5\)) is external** — Paper 33 §3 / V′ Face
  A's irreducibly-external bit. The program's two orientation data
  have opposite status.

**Strength gradient (anti-overclaim spine).**  From most to least
robust:

- **\([P]\)-adjacent — existence of a definite-sign arrow.**  Needs
  only \(m^2_{\text{simplex}}\ge 0\) (Paper 20 Rmk 2.2, [P]) plus the
  channel being non-invertible. Survives almost every degradation.
- **\([P]\)-adjacent — the H-theorem / second law.**  The
  monotone-metric contraction = DPI is a theorem *given* the projection
  is a CPTP map; it inherits exactly the Paper 18 §6 Petz–Bures finite
  check (no new audit), the same check the general-covariance analog
  of §5.A leans on.
- **\([A]\) — the causal trichotomy as a partition.**  That the
  residual sign partitions directions into three classes consistent
  with Face A's local-Casimir determinant-sign structure.
- **\([C]\), most fragile — the specific causal labelling.**  Which
  sign is spacelike-candidate vs timelike-candidate, and that null =
  exactly-vanishing residual = the local-Casimir asymptote locus. The
  sharpest, most testable, most falsifiable joint.

**Degradation ladder (matched-pair, both negative branches
pre-claimed).**

- *S′'s manifold-level geometric reading is already refuted* (§13.2);
  Face A's hyperboloid in this corollary is the §13.2A local-Casimir
  hyperboloid only. The trichotomy is hosted at the local-tangent
  layer.
- *If the projection channel is not monotone-contracting* (not CPTP /
  Bures not non-increasing under it): the H-theorem half collapses to
  "no derived second law"; this also threatens Paper 18 §6 Petz–Bures,
  so it is tied to an existing node, not a new risk.
- *If U′ closes negative on all three targets*: the rate-ratio
  constants vanish but the arrow's *existence and direction* survive
  — they need only \(m^2\ge 0\), not U′.  Target 1 has already fired
  the negative branch on \(\mathbb Z/6\) (Cor 6.3 (T1)); the arrow is
  unaffected.
- *If the causal labelling is refuted* (the audit below): the
  trichotomy reverts to "the residual is a leakage scalar with a sign,
  no causal labels." The arrow proper (existence + direction) and the
  H-theorem core stand. Both branches pre-claimed.

Every path lands on a *stated* weaker result, never on silence
(K/L / Paper 33 Q6 matched-pair discipline).

**Firewall compliance (inherited from U′ §1.4).**  Admissible: the
*existence* of the arrow, its *direction*, the *sign* of the decay
exponent, *ratios* of decay rates across conductor sectors, and the
*structural* trichotomy. **Not admissible**: any lifetime, any
absolute decay rate, any numerical relaxation time — these are
dimensionful and out of scope by §11.2, exactly as the Compton
wavelength is. *The arrow's direction is inferable; its rate is not.*

*Audit obligations (settle the [A]/[C] tiers; no new analytic
machinery beyond what is already on the ledger).*

1. **Monotone-contraction / H-theorem audit (settles the arrow
   half).**  Confirm the diagonal/measurement projection is a CPTP map
   under which the Bures/SLD metric is non-increasing — i.e. that the
   arrow's H-theorem is exactly Petz monotonicity specialized to this
   channel, discharged by the *existing* Paper 18 §6 Petz–Bures
   finite check. No new analytic machinery; flag for joint discharge
   with the general-covariance audit (same theorem).
2. **Causal-labelling audit (settles the fragile [C]; the real
   falsifier lives here).**  Verify the residual-sign partition is
   consistent with Face A's local-Casimir determinant-sign trichotomy
   and that null = exactly-vanishing residual = the asymptote locus. A
   single counterexample (positive residual on both sides of the cone,
   or null \(\ne\) vanishing-residual) refutes the labelling and
   triggers the pre-claimed reversion to "signed leakage scalar, no
   causal labels." Finite check on the \(\mathbb Z/6\) packets; may
   reuse the Paper 32 Appendix F integrator and the Paper 20 packet
   structure on \(\{A_2, A_3, M\}\). \(\square\)

### 9.7 The Einstein-like equation as the magnitude-law of the projection non-closure

**Corollary 9.10 (The Einstein-like equation as the magnitude-law of
the projection non-closure) [C, reduced; three GR content-pillars
inherited [P], only the fourth (sourcing) conjectured].**

*The four-pillar accounting (the de-risking move, stated first).*
General Relativity's actual content is four content-pillars, not the
slogan "gravity is curvature." Three are already proven in this
program:

- **(i) metric structure with no prior geometry.** **[P]** — the
  metric is the Fisher second cumulant \(g=\nabla^{(2)}\Phi\) (§4
  Theorem 4.1); uniqueness via the Chentsov/Petz monotone-metric
  general-covariance analog (Paper 18 §6 / Remark 6.1a role (ii)).
- **(ii) both sides divergence-free (Bianchi ↔ local
  conservation).** **[P]** — \(\nabla\!\cdot T=0\) is the
  Filippov/fundamental identity of the Nambu–Fisher bracket (§5
  Theorem 5.1). This is already proven; R′ does not conjecture it.
- **(iv) the field equation is the stationarity of one action.**
  **[P]** — \(\Phi\) is the categorical effective action; the cubic
  Noether/force law is its stationarity; the doubled space is Kähler
  with global potential \(\Phi\) (§3 Claim 3.1 + Remark 3.2 / the
  Zhang–Li construction). Already structural; R′ does not conjecture
  it.

The Einstein-like equation R′ conjectures only the fourth content
pillar:

- **(iii) curvature is *sourced* by stress–energy.** **[C], reduced.**
  Schematically
  \[
  \delta\mathcal R_{\text{proj}}\;\propto\;T^{(4)},
  \]
  where \(\delta\mathcal R_{\text{proj}}\) is the deviation of the
  projected back-path's Fisher/Bures curvature from the *fixed*
  Hellinger-sphere constant-curvature value, and \(T^{(4)}=
  m^2_{\text{simplex}}\) is the order-4 cumulant defect / jerk
  (Paper 20 Definition 2.1).

**Three of GR's four content-pillars are already [P] in this program;
R′ conjectures only the fourth, the sourcing, with a hard falsifier.**
This is the single most important sentence of the corollary: it
collapses R′ from "we conjecture an Einstein equation wholesale" to
"we conjecture one link, three pillars already proven."

*The LHS shape is forced, not chosen.* The divergence-free curvature
combination that can sit opposite a \(\nabla\!\cdot T=0\) source is
forced by the *same* Filippov / fundamental identity that delivers
pillar (ii). So the "Einstein-tensor analog" on the left is selected
by an *already-[P]* structural constraint, not posited. R′ inherits
the *shape* of both sides; it conjectures only that the
proportionality channel between them is non-trivial.

*Magnitude-law of the W′ object (ripe, not cold).* R′ is *the
magnitude-law of the very projection non-closure whose sign-law is
W′* (§9.6 Corollary 9.9 / item W′; see also §5 Remark 5.2A). One
projection non-closure, two readings: its *sign* is the arrow of
time (W′); its *magnitude* is the curvature-defect / gravity-
adjacent stress (R′ here). R′ inherits W′'s entire scaffold — same
local-Casimir Face A host, same Face C \(\hbar\)-clock, same U′
firewall, same Paper 18 §6 monotonicity node, same §5 non-closure
object. The only new conjectural surface is the *functional form of
the sourcing*; everything else is inherited.

*Discharge of the §3 promissory note.* §3 Claim 3.1 / Remark 3.2
asserts informally that "the relations physics must posit (mass
sources curvature; gravity is geometry) become *identities of the
tower*." Corollary 9.10 is exactly the rigorous, tiered, falsifiable,
firewall-bound form of that promissory note. It converts "mass
sources curvature becomes an identity of the tower" into a stated
[C, reduced] relation with an explicit falsifier and a Newton-
constant firewall. R′ discharges §3; it does not extend the program's
claim surface.

*The Newton-constant trap (the U′-analog; binding, do-not-cut).* The
proportionality has a coefficient. The Newton-constant analog — its
dimensionful magnitude — is **permanently out of scope by §11.2**,
*exactly* as the metric value of \(c\) (§9.3), the magnitude of
\(\hbar\) (§9.4), and the Compton wavelength (§11.2.1 item U′) are.
The Newton constant is to R′ what the Compton wavelength is to U′:
the most natural-seeming target and a firewall trap. Admissible
content is only (a) the *structural form* of the sourcing (that a
non-trivial functional channel exists), and (b) any *dimensionless /
conductor-fixed* content of the proportionality — a U′-target
question, strictly guarded. **No value of \(G\), no curvature
magnitude, no length, no mass, ever.**

**Falsifier (the spine of this reduced [C]; matched-pair, both
branches pre-claimed).** If \(\delta\mathcal R_{\text{proj}}\) is
identically functionally *independent* of \(T^{(4)}\) — i.e. the
Hellinger-sphere curvature is rigidly constant under every admissible
projected back-path, with no functional channel from \(T^{(4)}\) to
\(\delta\mathcal R_{\text{proj}}\) — then there is no sourcing, the
Einstein-like equation does not exist, and the gravity homolog is
**permanently capped at the fixed-background tier**. That negative
branch is pre-claimed (K/L, Paper 33 Q6 discipline). Conversely, any
non-trivial functional dependence
\(\delta\mathcal R_{\text{proj}}=F(T^{(4)})\), \(F\not\equiv0\),
*confirms the sourcing* and is itself a clean structural result —
still **not** General Relativity (see §11.1 below).

**Strength gradient (anti-overclaim spine).**

- **[P], inherited, survives everything.** Pillars (i) metric =
  cumulant (§4), (ii) Bianchi/Filippov (§5 Thm 5.1),
  (iv) action-stationarity (§3) are independent of R′ and stand
  regardless.
- **[P] core of the matched object.**
  \(m^2_{\text{simplex}}\ge 0\) (Paper 20 Rmk 2.2): the magnitude
  object is sign-definite, so even pre-sourcing the stress is
  bounded-below positive — no ghost/tachyon on the LHS source.
- **[C], reduced — the sole conjecture.** The sourcing functional
  channel \(\delta\mathcal R_{\text{proj}}=F(T^{(4)})\),
  \(F\not\equiv0\).

**Degradation paths.** If R′ is falsified (fixed-background cap),
INSERT 01's gravity homolog stands but permanently static; W′ (the
arrow) is *unaffected* (it needs only the sign, never the
magnitude-sourcing). If U′ closes negative (no conductor-fixed
rational), the proportionality has no inferable rational content but
the structural sourcing form can still hold with a non-combinatoric
coefficient (firewall-excluded *as an inferable constant*, but
structural sourcing not refuted). Every path lands on a *stated*
weaker result, never silence.

**Audit obligations (move the [C] toward decision; mostly inherited).**

1. **Sourcing-channel audit (settles R′; the falsifier check).**
   Determine whether \(\delta\mathcal R_{\text{proj}}\) has a
   non-trivial functional dependence on \(T^{(4)}\) on admissible
   projected back-paths of the \(\mathbb Z/6\) row, or is identically
