### 9.9 Exhibit E1 — GR's four content-pillars vs. the categorical program (presentational)

> **Exhibit E1. General Relativity's four content-pillars vs. the
> categorical program.** *(Asserts only already-tiered facts;
> presentational; not a primed claim letter and not citable as a
> result.)*

| GR content pillar | GR's epistemic status | Program homolog | Program tier | Internal source |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **(i)** A metric structure with no prior geometry | **postulated** (general covariance) | metric = Fisher second cumulant \(g=\nabla^{(2)}\Phi\); uniqueness via the Chentsov/Petz monotone-metric theorem (general-covariance analog) | **[P]** | §4 Thm 4.1; Paper 18 §6 Rmk 6.1a role (ii) |
| **(ii)** Both sides divergence-free (Bianchi ↔ local conservation) | identity + **posited** \(\nabla\!\cdot T=0\) | \(\nabla\!\cdot T=0\) is the Filippov / fundamental identity of the Nambu–Fisher bracket | **[P]** | §5 Thm 5.1 |
| **(iv)** Field equation = stationarity of one action | **posited** (Einstein–Hilbert action) | \(\Phi\) = categorical effective action; cubic force law = its stationarity; doubled space Kähler with potential \(\Phi\) | **[P]** | §3 Claim 3.1 / Rmk 3.2 (Zhang–Li) |
| **(iii)** Curvature is *sourced* by stress–energy | **posited** (the Einstein equation; constant \(G\)) | \(\delta\mathcal R_{\text{proj}}\propto T^{(4)}\); coupling magnitude out of scope (§11.2) | **[C], reduced** (falsifiable; 3 pillars inherited [P]) | R′ / §9.7 Cor 9.10 |

**Epistemic note (accurate, not overclaimed).**  *General Relativity
postulates general covariance, the conservation law, and the field
equation. The categorical program proves three of GR's four
content-pillars and, for the fourth, offers a falsifiable conjecture
rather than a postulate.* The program's weakest pillar — (iii), [C] —
is a *falsifiable* conjecture with an explicit falsifier and a
fixed-background-cap negative branch, whereas GR's corresponding
content is a *postulate*, not a falsifiable derivation within GR.
This is an accurate epistemic observation about *structure*; **not** a
claim that the program "does GR better."

**Caption (mandatory, unsoftenable, do-not-cut — Exhibit E1 is the
highest-skim-risk artifact in the program; without this caption it
reads as "GR derived").** *Exhibit E1 asserts only already-tiered
internal facts. Three pillars are [P] within the program's own scope;
pillar (iii) is a falsifiable [C] conjecture (R′) whose dimensionful
coupling — the Newton-constant analog — is permanently out of scope
(§11.2). The program does **not** derive General Relativity, Newton's
constant, spacetime gravitation, or a physical field equation, even
if R′ confirms. The exhibit displays the projection-closure *form* of
a GR-shaped structure and its guardrail; it is not a derivation of
gravity. Positioning is against the emergent-gravity school (§11.1).*
An exhibit shipped without this caption is a guardrail violation —
cut, do not edit. E1 is classified in §12 as an **Exhibit
(presentational)**, *not* a primed claim letter; it asserts nothing
new and must not be cited as a result.

### 9.10 The Raychaudhuri focusing scalar localizes onto the projection-closure residual

**Corollary 9.12 (The Raychaudhuri focusing scalar is the
projection-closure residual; the shear–rotation sector is a
pre-claimed structural boundary) [A] on a [P] hinge (Paper 20 Rmk
2.2); one pre-claimed [C-boundary]; adds no new conjectural surface
— joint (i) inherits R′].**

*Raychaudhuri stripped to its joints.*  The Raychaudhuri equation for
a geodesic congruence with expansion \(\theta\), shear
\(\sigma_{ab}\), vorticity \(\omega_{ab}\), tangent \(u^a\), affine
parameter \(\lambda\), dimension \(n\),
\[
\frac{d\theta}{d\lambda}
= -\frac{\theta^{2}}{n-1}
\;-\;\sigma_{ab}\sigma^{ab}
\;+\;\omega_{ab}\omega^{ab}
\;-\;R_{ab}\,u^{a}u^{b},
\]
has, for unification purposes, **three joints**: (i) a
curvature-contraction object \(R_{ab}u^au^b\); (ii) a non-negativity
condition on it (the energy condition, which makes gravity
attractive); (iii) irreversible focusing to a caustic. The program
realizes all three on a single object — the projection-closure
residual \(T^{(4)}=m^2_{\text{simplex}}\) — and owns the
shear–rotation tensor sector **not at all, by construction**.

**Joint (i) — the curvature-contraction object is the R′ defect ([C], reduced).**
The Ricci-contraction \(R_{ab}u^au^b\) that focuses the congruence
maps to the program's projected curvature defect
\(\delta\mathcal R_{\text{proj}}\) of §9.7 Corollary 9.10 / item R′:
its sourcing law is \([C]\) reduced, three GR content-pillars
inherited [P], only the sourcing conjectured. *No new conjectural
surface is opened by the Raychaudhuri reading* — joint (i) inherits
R′ wholesale, including its falsifier (fixed-background cap) and its
Newton-constant firewall trap.

**Joint (ii) — the energy condition is the program's proven
\(m^2_{\text{simplex}}\ge 0\) ([P]).**  The non-negativity
\(R_{ab}u^au^b\ge 0\) — the condition that makes gravity *attractive*,
the physically hard part of the focusing theorem — is exactly the
program's Paper 20 Remark 2.2 inequality, the same [P] hinge that
underwrites W′ and X′. **GR imports the energy condition from the
matter sector (a posited property of \(T_{\mu\nu}\)); the program's
analog is a proven non-negativity of its own mass object** (the same
epistemic asymmetry as pillar (i) of Exhibit E1: where GR posits,
the program proves). The hard part of the focusing theorem sits on
the program's **[P]** hinge, not its [C] conjecture.

**Joint (iii) — irreversible focusing is the W′ data-processing
contraction ([P]-adjacent).**  Caustic formation in Raychaudhuri
(finite-\(\lambda\) focusing, \(\theta\to-\infty\)) is the program's
irreversible distinguishability collapse under the projection
channel: the diagonal/measurement channel is non-invertible, the
SLD/Bures metric contracts under it (Petz monotonicity, Paper 18 §6),
the contraction is the data-processing inequality, hence an H-theorem
— concretely \(P_{\text{survive}}\sim\exp(-c\,m^2_{\text{simplex}}\,t)\)
is the monotone, irreversible loss of distinguishability. A
data-processing inequality *is* a focusing theorem in
information-geometric clothing: monotone contraction of a metric is
exactly the statement that a congruence cannot defocus on its own.
Inherits the W′ [P] core and the Paper 18 §6 node; no new audit.

**The synthesis (one object, three readings).**  The second-law ⟺
energy-condition ⟺ focusing linkage that underlies the
Hawking–Penrose singularity theorems is, in this program, **one
object read three ways**: sign = arrow (W′), non-negativity of the
magnitude = energy condition (the Paper 20 Rmk 2.2 [P] hinge, the
joint (ii) homolog), magnitude = the Einstein-like source (R′; the
joint (i) homolog). The coupling — the proven sign disciplining the
conjectured magnitude to be focusing-positive — is the X′ corollary
of §9.8. *The W′/X′ cluster is the singularity-theorem
focusing–energy-condition linkage seen from another side* — a
UEA-class structural recurrence, **not** a derivation of Raychaudhuri,
a singularity theorem, or gravitational collapse.

**Scope boundary (pre-claimed, [C-boundary], heaviest do-not-cut;
the matched-pair move).**  Raychaudhuri's full content includes the
**shear and rotation terms**, \(-\sigma_{ab}\sigma^{ab}\) (shear
*adds* to focusing) and \(+\omega_{ab}\omega^{ab}\) (rotation
*opposes* it). The program owns these **not at all, by
construction**, because it has a projection channel on a categorical
simplex, *not* a congruence in a spacetime manifold. This is not a
missing lemma and not a deferred audit; it is a structural boundary
— the Raychaudhuri analog of the §11.2 dimensional firewall and of
the §11.1 anti-overclaim scope on R′. **A confirmed focusing-scalar
homolog is still not Raychaudhuri, still not a singularity theorem,
still not gravitational collapse — it is a structural
sign-and-contraction linkage on an information-geometric simplex.**
Any draft that softens this paragraph, or presents the
focusing-scalar homolog without it, is a guardrail violation and must
be cut, not edited.

**Strength gradient (anti-overclaim spine).**

- **[P], inherited** — joint (ii): the energy-condition homolog is
  \(m^2_{\text{simplex}}\ge 0\) (Paper 20 Rmk 2.2). *The hard part of
  the focusing theorem is proven where GR posits it.* Single most
  robust statement of the corollary.
- **[P]-adjacent** — joint (iii): irreversible focusing = W′ DPI,
  inheriting the Paper 18 §6 Petz–Bures node.
- **[A] on the [P] hinge** — the coupling (sign disciplines
  magnitude) is X′; the synthesis above inherits X′'s tier exactly.
- **[C], reduced** — joint (i): the curvature-defect *sourcing* is
  R′; the only conjectural surface, with R′'s own falsifier
  (fixed-background cap).
- **[C-boundary], pre-claimed negative by construction** — the
  shear–rotation sector: owned not at all, stated, not a gap.

**Degradation.** If R′ is falsified (fixed-background cap), joint (i)
loses its sourcing law, but joints (ii)–(iii) are unaffected — the
energy-condition homolog and irreversible-focusing homolog need only
the [P] sign and the monotone channel. If W′'s causal labelling is
refuted, joint (iii) reverts to the bare [P] \(m^2\ge 0\) monotone-
loss core, which still supplies irreversible focusing. If X′ is
refuted, the coupling weakens but joints (i)–(iii) individually stand;
the synthesis reverts to "three separate homologs" rather than "one
object, three readings." The §1.6 boundary does not degrade — it is
pre-claimed negative.

**Audit obligations (mostly inherited; one process check).**

1. *Joint-localization consistency audit (settles the [A] core).*
   Verify (a) R′'s defect is the homolog of \(R_{ab}u^au^b\)
   (inherits R′'s audit, no new analytic obligation); (b) Paper 20
   Rmk 2.2 is the correct homolog of the energy-condition
   non-negativity; (c) W′ DPI is the correct homolog of irreversible
   focusing (inherits Paper 18 §6). Bookkeeping consistency over
   already-tiered items.
2. *Boundary-discipline check (process, not mathematical).* Confirm
   Corollary 9.12 never appears without the shear–rotation boundary
   paragraph and that §11.1 carries it unsoftened. A 9.12 shipped
   without its boundary is a guardrail violation — cut, do not edit. \(\square\)

