## 10.5 The Unification Thesis (added v0.2.5)

> *Take a step back. T0–T10 are a solid framework. What is Paper 32 touching
> but not claiming? What boundaries should it be crossing?*

Reread through the T-series substrate (§2.5), Paper 32's central claims
compose into a unification thesis the previous draft *touched* but did not
*name*. Draft 0.2.5 names it. The discipline rails of §11.1 / §11.2 / §11.4
preserve unchanged; what changes is that the framework's structural-shape
relationship to perturbative quantum gravity is now stated as a thesis with
explicit dictionary entries, rather than left as a series of correspondence
remarks scattered across Papers 32 / 33 / 41 / 44 / 46 / 47 / 48 / 49.

### 10.5.1 The pushback that forces the section

A reader of v0.2.5 reasonably asks: *"gravity localizes to the
multiplicative units" — as in Quantum Gravity?* The honest answer is yes
in the structural-form sense, no in the physical sense — and the
discipline rails are *heavier* at the threshold of naming the thesis than
they were when the framework merely touched it. §10.5 makes the
structural-form thesis explicit and the firewall on the physical-form
claim heavier; the two are inseparable.

### 10.5.2 What the framework is touching (the six load-bearing recognitions)

Paper 32 §9's "one lift, four faces" — Lorentzian signature, nonabelian
gauge restoration, the imaginary \(i\), the invariant speed \(c\) — sits
inside a larger structural picture that the T-series substrate makes
explicit. Six load-bearing recognitions:

**(F0) The Bures lift IS the canonical complex-projective amplitude
bundle.** T7 §1 Theorem 1.1: Born closure factors *uniquely* as
\(\pi_{\text{Born}}=\mu_{\text{toric}}\circ\text{Hopf}\circ\text{rad}\)
through \(S^{2N-1}\to\mathbb{CP}^{N-1}\to\Delta^{N-1}\). The "Bures
lift" of Paper 18 is *the* (not "a") complex-projective amplitude bundle;
the Bures metric is the Fubini–Study metric pulled back to density
matrices. "One lift" means *one* \(\mathbb{CP}^{N-1}\), uniquely.

**(F1) Quantization IS the Kummer cover.** T7 §5 Theorem 5.2 + §3.4
Proposition 3.7(c): at integer gauge \(\beta=m\), the closure-diagonal
\(\mathcal M_z(m,c)\) is a section of a non-trivial \(\mu_N\)-cover of
\(\mathbb{CP}^{N-1}\) iff \(N\nmid m\). The cover is the literal Galois-
theoretic content of "quantization": moduli of additive characters become
multi-valued upon lifting to complex amplitudes, with the per-coordinate
deck group \(\mu_N/\mu_{\gcd(N,m)}\). This sharpens Paper 44's
"quantization is forced by representation theory" (Theorem 8.1): the
*mechanism* by which quantization is forced is precisely the
non-triviality of the Kummer cover at the cubic gauge rung. **T7's
slogan — "quantization is the cover" — is the load-bearing identity.**

**(F2) Decoherence IS closure of phase.** T7 §4.2 Theorem 4.1: modulus
restriction \(z\mapsto|z|\) reduces the complex apex generator
\(\mathcal M_z(\beta,c)\) to the real-positive apex
\(\mathcal M_{|z|}(\beta,c)\) on the modulus ledger. Paper 32 §9.6
Corollary 9.9's dephasing channel \(\mathcal P\) is the density-matrix
version (T7 §4.5). The "diagonal/measurement projection" is *literally*
the section of the Hopf+toric fibrations that picks zero-phase
representatives. T7's other slogan — "decoherence is closure of phase"
— is the load-bearing identity.

**(F3) Gravity is the multiplicative-unit-indexed additive sector.**
§2.5.4 / Observation 2.5.4 / ledger item GG: at primorial \(\mathbb Z/P_k\),
the conductor-\(P_k\) carry packet \(M\) — which supports the gravity-
adjacent residual (Paper 32 Theorem 6.2 [P]; the Hawking-radiation-analog
of Paper 20 §3; the simplex-mass term \(m^2_{\text{simplex}}\)) — is
index-identical, as a subset of \(\mathbb Z/P_k\), to the multiplicative-
unit subgroup \((\mathbb Z/P_k)^\times\). **Gravity localizes to the
units of the conductor row.**

**(F4) The matter / gauge sector is the non-unit additive sector.**
The single-prime axes \(A_{p_i}\) (Cartan / \(\mathfrak{u}(1)\)-flow
sectors of Paper 17) and the proper-divisor packets \(H_d\) for
\(d\mid N\), \(d>1\), \(d<N\), are indexed by the non-units of
\(\mathbb Z/N\). These are the kinematic sectors (Paper 47's V) where
the cubic Noether projection closes (Paper 32 Theorem 6.2). **Matter
localizes to the non-units of the conductor row.**

**(F5) Finite Dirichlet polynomials are the natural "QG observables"
of the framework.** T8 §5 defines the finite Dirichlet polynomial
\(L_x(\beta,\chi):=\sum_{n=1}^N\chi(n)/x_n^\beta\). By T8 Proposition
5.2, \(L_x(-\beta,\chi)\) is, up to geometric-mean normalization, the
multiplicative apex \(\mathcal D_x(\beta,\bar\chi)\) on units (T8 §2).
Since the gravity-adjacent residual lives on units (F3), the natural
propagator/correlator structure of the gravity sector is encoded in
finite Dirichlet polynomials. The RH bridge of Paper 22 / Paper 32 §7
acquires its sharp form: *the all-order Noether–Weil positivity of these
polynomials is the positive-energy condition on the gravity sector*.

