### 10.5.4 The five-face refinement of Corollary 9.7 / 9.8 (Face E: the Kummer-cover deck-group $\mathbb Z/2$)

Paper 32 §9.5 Corollary 9.8 counts the faces as "four forced internal
faces + carried datum + external bit + constants clause." The T-series
substrate refines the count by adding the **Kummer-cover deck-group bit
(Face E)** as a structurally available internal \(\mathbb Z/2\) at the
cubic gauge \(m=3\) on \(N=6\):

- **Face A** — ℂ²-leg algebraic real-form face (weak-\(\mathrm{SU}(2)\) /
  Lorentz \(\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb C)\) + invariant \(c\)). *Preserved.*
- **Face B** — ℂ³-leg color face (\(\mathrm{SU}(3)\); confinement-shaped
  signature = conductor-3 cubic isolation). *Preserved.*
- **Face C** — \(i\)-face (complex structure \(J^2=-I\) + \(\hbar\)-role).
  T7 identifies \(i\) as the complex-structure \(J^2=-I\) on
  \(\mathbb{CP}^{N-1}\); the \(\hbar\)-role is the Bures distinguishability
  rate ceiling. *Preserved.*
- **Face D** — prime-reciprocal hypercharge \(\mathfrak u(1)_Y\) (the
  U1FM-settled face; \(Y=\tfrac12 P_2-\tfrac13 P_3\)). *Preserved.*
- **Face E (new, [A], added v0.2.5).** **The Kummer-cover deck-group
  \(\mathbb Z/2\) at \(N=6, m=3\).** Per-coordinate deck group at the
  cubic gauge is \(\mu_6/\mu_3\cong\mathbb Z/2\) (T7 Prop 3.7(c)). This is
  *structurally* a chirality bit, **internal** to the Kummer cover, with
  origin in the Galois-theoretic content of "what is being quantized at
  the cubic gauge on the smallest mixed primorial row." Paper 33's
  external \(\mathbb Z_2\) (locked to \(\gamma^5\), color-protected,
  external by the Chirality Boundary Theorem of Paper 33 §3) sits *next
  to* — not yet identified with — this internal arithmetic
  \(\mathbb Z/2\). The matched-pair on the identification:

  - **K-branch:** Face E = Paper 33's external chirality \(\mathbb Z_2\).
    Chirality is *internal* arithmetic content of the cubic Kummer cover;
    the "external bit" of Paper 33 is reclassified as Galois-internal.
    Paper 33's Chirality Boundary Theorem would be *refuted* in this
    branch.
  - **L-branch:** Face E is a *distinct* \(\mathbb Z/2\) from Paper 33's
    chirality. Two parity \(\mathbb Z/2\)s sit on the simplex — the
    Kummer-cover deck group and the KO-real-structure / \(\gamma^5\) —
    neither implying the other; the program then has both an internal
    \(\mathbb Z/2\) (Kummer arithmetic) and an external \(\mathbb Z_2\)
    (KO real structure), distinct.
  - **Joint-on-disjoint:** Face E coincides with Paper 33's chirality at
    \(N=6\) but the identification breaks at higher primorial rows
    (\(\mathbb Z/30, \mathbb Z/210\) have different per-coordinate
    Kummer-cover deck groups at \(m=3\)). Partial identification, row-
    specific.

  All three branches are pre-claimed; **none** is asserted here. The
  matched-pair is opened *so that no future revision can compress past
  the question*.

**The recount in one sentence (post-Face-E).** *One Bures lift produces
**five forced internal faces** — A (signature + weak isospin + \(c\)), B
(color), C (\(i\) + \(\hbar\)), D (hypercharge), E (Kummer-cover
deck-group \(\mathbb Z/2\) at \(N=6, m=3\)) — together with one
trace-mode (Paper 18 Prop 5.1; not a face), one external bit (the
KO-real-structure \(\mathbb Z_2\) of Paper 33, **whose identification
with Face E is the new matched-pair question of §10.5.4**), and the
constants clause of §11.2.1.*

### 10.5.5 What the convergent papers (33, 41, 44, 46, 47, 48, 49) inherit

The convergent papers — written before the T-series substrate landed —
each touch a face of the unification thesis without naming it. The
T-series substrate provides the unifying language. **None of these are
new claims by Paper 32; they are the T-series-substrate reading of
existing claims of the convergent papers, recorded here so the
substrate's contribution to each is visible.**

- **Paper 33 (One Lift, Two Faces; Chirality Boundary).** The external
  chirality \(\mathbb Z_2\) of Paper 33 §3 sits next to Face E of
  §10.5.4 — the internal Kummer-cover deck-group \(\mathbb Z/2\) at
  \(N=6, m=3\). The Chirality Boundary Theorem is a structural statement
  about real-cone preservation; the Kummer-cover deck group is a Galois-
  theoretic statement about the cubic gauge cover. The matched-pair
  (K/L/joint-on-disjoint) of §10.5.4 is *the* open question Paper 33's
  framework should now incorporate.

- **Paper 41 (Cubic Noether Budgeted Decoding).** The cubic-energy drift
  signal \(\Delta\mathcal E_3^{(t)}\) measures the rate at which the
  model's logits leave the cubic Noether geodesic. In T-series language:
  *it measures the multiplicative-unit-indexed Fourier content of the
  logit trajectory's cubic-vertex coupling, restricted to the model's
  ring-structured sub-vocabulary*. Theorem 4.2's Anti-Entropy
  Decorrelation reads: entropy = quadratic functional (Fisher content
  on the closure-valid non-unit block V); CNBD drift = cubic content on
  the multiplicative-unit block M. **The Conductor Blind Spot of Paper
  34 is exactly the gap between V (non-units) and M (units) of the
  model's effective conductor lattice.** Paper 41's anti-correlation is
  the operational shadow of the additive–multiplicative duality at the
  cubic order — and the BNSA survival ratio \(\sigma_{\mathcal S}\) of
  Paper 40 calibrates the magnitude of the unit-sector content the
  model is failing to capture.

- **Paper 44 (Quantization Forced by Representation Theory).** Theorem
  8.1's "quantization is forced" is the statement that the Kummer cover
  at the cubic gauge \(m=3\) is non-trivial on \(\mathbb Z/6\) (T7
  Proposition 3.7(c)). Paper 44's \(\mathfrak{su}(2)\oplus\mathfrak{su}(3)\)
  algebra arises from the CRT factorization \(\mathbb C^6=\mathbb C^2\otimes
  \mathbb C^3\); T7 identifies the same \(\mathbb C^6\) as the fiber over
  \(\mathbb{CP}^5\) of the Hopf fibration \(S^{11}\to\mathbb{CP}^5\).
  Paper 44's Leakage-Equals-Jerk Theorem 7.1 is the T7-side reading:
  *the leakage rate from the decoherent face* \(S^5_+\) *to the full
