### 10.5.6 Boundaries Paper 32 should now cross (and the firewall that stays)

With the T-series substrate explicit, three boundaries Paper 32 should
cross — and one it should not.

**Should cross (added v0.2.5).**

**(B1) Name the thesis.** Paper 32 should explicitly state, as Thesis in
§10.5.3, that *the categorical-simplex framework is the realization of
the QG gravity-matter decoupling problem on a finite-arithmetic
substrate*. The discipline rails of §11.1 / §11.2 / §11.4 preserve; what
changes is that the framework has crossed from "discharging the *form*
of the question" (Paper 31 §13 guardrail, v0.2.4 framing) to "providing
a finite-arithmetic substrate where the question can be *answered* in
the structural-form sense." The substrate is: the gauge corridor
(T0/T10) + the conductor lattice (T3) + the Kummer cover (T7) + the
multiplicative apex (T8) + the Helmert/Fourier transfer matrix (T9).
The answer (at \(\mathbb Z/6\), cubic order) is: arithmetic V ⊥ M
decoupling, forced by Pontryagin character orthogonality on the
additive–multiplicative partition of \(\mathbb Z/N\).

**(B2) Open the Face E matched-pair (§10.5.4).** The Kummer-cover deck-
group \(\mathbb Z/2\) at \(N=6, m=3\) is a structurally available
internal chirality candidate. The matched-pair K / L / joint-on-disjoint
of §10.5.4 is opened so chirality acquires *two* candidate origins —
Paper 33's external \(\gamma^5\) and the internal Kummer-cover deck-
group — without prematurely deciding. *This is a new claim line opened
by v0.2.5.*

**(B3) Name "arithmetic quantum gravity at finite primorial" as the
program's structural-shape claim.** This is what Paper 47's
correspondence-language framing was already touching but not naming.
The T-series substrate makes the naming honest: the program's gravity
sector lives on the multiplicative units; the Pontryagin / Gauss-sum
bridge (T8 §4) is the framework's connection to the classical analytic-
number-theoretic content of Dirichlet \(L\)-functions; the RH bridge of
Paper 22 is the framework's positive-energy condition; the Kummer cover
of T7 is the framework's quantization. "Arithmetic quantum gravity at
finite primorial" is the framework's name *for itself*, with the
program's positioning against physical QG (§11.1) unchanged.

**Should NOT cross.**

**(B-fail) Do not promote any face to a physical claim.** The Lorentzian
signature is local-tangent (§13.2A). The "gravity" is structural-form
(Paper 47 / §10.5.3). The "quantization" is Kummer-cover (T7). None of
these promote to physical claims about spacetime, gravitons, Planck
scales, or quantum gravity at high energies. *The §11.2 firewall is
strengthened, not weakened, by the naming*: no Newton constant, no
Planck length, no Compton wavelength, no \(G\), no \(\Lambda\), no
graviton mass, no curvature in meters, no cosmological time in seconds,
no anything dimensionful. The unification thesis raises the stakes
because the structural form has now been named; the firewall protects
the framework from the natural reader-mistake of reading the structural-
form claim as a physical claim.

### 10.5.7 The one-sentence answer

> ***Q: As in Quantum Gravity?***
>
> ***A:** In the structural-form sense, yes — at finite primorial, on the
> categorical simplex, with the gravity sector localized to the
> multiplicative-unit subgroup* \((\mathbb Z/P_k)^\times\) *of the
> conductor row, with quantization realized as the Kummer cover at the
> cubic gauge* \(m=3\) *with per-coordinate deck group*
> \(\mu_N/\mu_{\gcd(N,m)}\)*, and with the gravity-matter decoupling
> forced by Pontryagin character orthogonality on the additive-vs-
> multiplicative partition of* \(\mathbb Z/N\)*. In the physical-
> Newtonian/Einsteinian/Planck sense, no — the §11.2 firewall is
> binding and no dimensionful coupling, no length scale, no graviton, no
> metric on a 4-manifold is derived, claimed, or accessible. The
> framework realizes the **structural shape** of QG on a finite
> arithmetic substrate where the question is answerable; it does not
> derive the **physical content** of QG and is not in the same
> competitive lane as perturbative-QG, asymptotic-safety, AdS/CFT,
> loop-quantum-gravity, causal-dynamical-triangulations, or string
> compactification.*

