**\(\mathbb Z/8\) is the period of real Bott periodicity in K-theory:**
\(KO^{-n}(\text{pt})=KO^{-n+8}(\text{pt})\). The Connes–Chamseddine
classification of finite spectral triples uses **KO-dimension mod 8**:

| KO-dim | \(J^2\) | \(JD\) | Algebra |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | \(+1\) | \(+DJ\) | \(\mathbb R\) |
| 1 | \(+1\) | \(-DJ\) | \(\mathbb R^2\) |
