## 11. Relationship to Newtonian Gravity and the Guardrails

Paper 31 §13: "projection-closure theory explains the *form* of the gravity
question, not gravity itself." This paper discharges that guardrail *partially
and by type*: the *form* of the gravity residual is now an explicit, localized,
bounded, falsifiable object on a named row, and its stability is identified with
a known deep positivity (Theorem 7.1). It does **not** claim a metric, a
stress-energy with the correct weak-field limit, lensing, or cosmology. The
ten boundary conditions of Paper 31 §13 remain open and are now reorganized as
tests of one object: the time-translation closure residual on the conductor-6
mode and its large-\(N\) scaling. Newtonian three-body chaos remains real
inside pairwise dynamics (Paper 28 §10); the new content is that the cross-prime
carry, not dynamical sensitivity, selects the gravity-adjacent sector.

### 11.1 Relation to emergent-gravity programs (and why the guardrail is the contribution)

There is a substantial, legitimate external lineage deriving gravitational
field equations from thermodynamic or information-theoretic premises: Jacobson's
derivation of the Einstein equation as an equation of state from the local
Clausius relation; Padmanabhan's thermodynamic-gravity and equipartition
program; Verlinde's entropic-gravity proposal; and, on the information-geometry
side, constructions in which an emergent metric is taken as an inverse Fisher
information matrix whose flow yields Einstein-form equations. We acknowledge
this lineage and *position against its strongest claim*. Even the most rigorous
member (Jacobson) does not deliver a metric that survives the full boundary
battery — weak-field limit, lensing, perihelion, gravitational-wave
propagation, cluster collisions, cosmological structure growth — without
additional input; the entropic and inverse-Fisher variants face known
empirical and consistency objections.

This is precisely why Paper 32 *does not* claim "gravity is the inverse Fisher
metric" and *does not* claim the Einstein equations are "natively recovered."
The contribution of this paper is the opposite epistemic move: not a faster
route to writing down \(R_{\mu\nu}-\tfrac12 R g_{\mu\nu}=8\pi T_{\mu\nu}\), but
a *closure certificate* that says when such a projection is even allowed, and a
proof that on \(R=\mathbb{Z}/6\mathbb{Z}\) the time-translation residual is
arithmetically localized, typed, bounded, and falsifiable rather than an
undifferentiated error term absorbed into an assumed metric. Where the
emergent-gravity school discharges the gravity question by *asserting* the
metric identification, this program discharges only the *form* of the question
and keeps the metric identification as an open, audited target (Paper 31 §13
guardrail; §13 here). Adopting the school's register would place this series
inside a crowded, contested field and forfeit its one structural advantage —
the certificate discipline. The guardrail is not timidity; it is the result.

**The anti-overclaim scope statement for R′ / §9.7 Corollary 9.10
(heaviest single edit of §11.1; unsoftenable, do-not-cut).**  Even if
the §9.7 Einstein-like equation R′ *confirms*, this program does
**not** derive General Relativity, a metric theory of gravitation,
Newton's constant, spacetime, or a physical field equation. A
confirmed R′ yields *a structural sourcing relation on the projected
channel of an information-geometric categorical simplex* — nothing
more. The program's positioning against the emergent-gravity school
is heaviest at R′ because it is the program's single most seductive
overclaim, and the contribution is the *guardrail*, not a gravity
derivation. The admissible claim is exactly: *the projection-closure
form of why a GR-shaped sourcing relation is (or is not) forced on
the simplex* — with three pillars inherited [P] (§4 metric =
cumulant; §5 Bianchi/Filippov; §3 action-stationarity), one pillar
[C] with a falsifier (sourcing, §9.7), and the coupling magnitude
permanently out of scope (§11.2, the Newton-constant U′-analog
trap). Any draft that softens this paragraph is a guardrail
violation and must be cut, not edited.

**The Raychaudhuri shear–rotation boundary (pre-claimed
[C-boundary]; second-heaviest §11.1 edit after R′; unsoftenable,
do-not-cut).**  The Raychaudhuri-focusing-scalar localization of §9.10
Corollary 9.12 / ledger item Z′ owns the *trace / focusing-scalar*
sector of Raychaudhuri (\(\theta\), \(R_{ab}u^au^b\), the
energy-condition non-negativity, the irreversible-focusing
contraction) at [P]/[A] on the Paper 20 Rmk 2.2 [P] hinge. It owns
the **shear–rotation tensor sector** —
\(-\sigma_{ab}\sigma^{ab}\), \(+\omega_{ab}\omega^{ab}\), and their
opposite signs in the focusing balance — **not at all, by
construction**: the program has a projection channel on a
categorical simplex, *not* a congruence in a spacetime manifold.
This is not a missing lemma and not a deferred audit; it is a
structural boundary, the Raychaudhuri analog of the §11.2
dimensional firewall and of the R′ anti-overclaim scope above. The
boundary is the contribution as much as the localization is: a
confirmed focusing-scalar homolog is *still not* Raychaudhuri,
*still not* a singularity theorem, *still not* gravitational
collapse — it is a structural sign-and-contraction linkage on an
information-geometric simplex. Stating this in matched-pair style
before any reader can present the shear–rotation absence as a
discovered gap is itself the deliverable: a pre-claimed structural
absence cannot later be banked as a quiet derivation. Any draft that
softens this paragraph, or presents Cor 9.12 / Z′ without it, is a
guardrail violation and must be cut, not edited. Raychaudhuri is a
*fifth probe* of the GR-recovery axis, not a *fifth pillar*;
Exhibit E1 stays at four pillars unchanged.

### 11.2 The dimensional firewall (what may and may not be predicted)

Because the simplex carries no length, time, or mass scale (Paper 20 §4), this
program may attempt **only dimensionless quantities fixed by conductor/cumulant
structure**. Anything carrying a unit — \(\hbar\), \(c\), \(G\), the Planck
scale, any absolute mass or length — is out of scope *by construction*, not by
caution. We state this explicitly as a firewall because it is the credibility
boundary for every constant the program may later discuss, and because adjacent
literature has crossed it (e.g. writing \(\text{mass}=\text{rest binding
energy}/c^2\) smuggles in \(c\)).

A subtle but admissible category sits inside the firewall: constants that are
**unity-by-construction**, whose content is the *theorem that they are unity
and invariant*, not a numerical value. Corollary 9.7's \(c\equiv1\) is the
archetype: the framework derives that an invariant speed *exists*, is
*frame-independent*, is the hyperboloid asymptote, and equals 1 in internal
units — and explicitly does **not** predict its metre/second value. This is the
correct template for any future constant claim: a *structural* prediction
(existence, invariance, a fixed rational ratio between sectors) is admissible;
a *dimensionful magnitude* never is. Candidate dimensionless targets consistent
with this firewall (the bare weak mixing angle / prime-reciprocal hypercharge
of Paper 33; structural integers such as the generation/dimension counts) are
to be pursued only under this rule and only as ratios or structural facts.

The firewall extends explicitly to the GR-shaped object opened as ledger item
R′ (§5.A) and to the \(i\)-face invariant of Corollary 9.7 Part 3 / §9.4
(ledger item T′). For R′: any inferable content is *structural* — the
relation form \(\delta\mathcal R_{\text{proj}}\propto T^{(4)}\), its
existence, the divergence-free shape on the left (forced by the Filippov
identity), and any conductor-fixed dimensionless proportionality — but the
*Newton-constant analog* (the dimensionful coupling magnitude) is permanently
out of scope, identical status to \(c\) and to any curvature scale. For T′:
the \(\hbar\)-role constant's existence, invariance, and conversion content
(Fisher clock ↔ phase clock) are admissible, identical-status to \(c\equiv1\);
the *numerical value of \(\hbar\) in any physical unit* is permanently out of
scope. The pattern is the same in every case: a *structural* prediction —
existence, invariance, the conversion it performs, a fixed rational ratio
between sectors — is admissible; a *dimensionful magnitude* never is. The
Newton constant, the Compton wavelength, the metre/second value of \(c\),
and any value of \(\hbar\) are all the same kind of firewall trap (the
U′-analog) and are excluded uniformly. The firewall extends in the same
form to the arrow / second-law content of Corollary 9.9 / ledger item
W′: arrow *direction*, *sign* of the decay exponent, and *ratios* of
decay rates across conductor sectors are structural and admissible; any
*lifetime*, any *absolute decay rate*, any *numerical relaxation time*
is dimensionful and out of scope by the same firewall, identical status
to the Compton wavelength. The arrow's direction is inferable; its rate
is not. The firewall extends identically to the §9.7 Einstein-like
equation R′: the *structural form* of the sourcing
\(\delta\mathcal R_{\text{proj}}\propto T^{(4)}\) and any
*conductor-fixed dimensionless* content of the proportionality are
askable; the *Newton-constant analog magnitude* of the coupling is
permanently out of scope, identical firewall status to \(c\), \(\hbar\),
and the Compton wavelength.

#### 11.2.1 Admissible scale-free targets of the \(c\)–\(\hbar\) pair (the three-target taxonomy of item U′)

With both paired conversion invariants now named — \(c\) on the signature
face (§9.3, Corollary 9.7 Parts 1–2) and the \(\hbar\)-role on the
imaginary-\(i\) face (§9.4, ledger item T′) — the firewall permits *exactly
one* constants question over the pair: which **dimensionless** combinations
of \(c\), \(\hbar\), and the conductor/cumulant combinatorics are
*structurally fixed*, with no free dimensionful input. Three candidate
targets are pre-enumerated so the question cannot later be drifted, and so
the discipline of §11.4 applies uniformly:

1. **Simplex-mass ratios across conductor sectors (Paper 20 native, would-be
   firewall-proof entry point).** Ratios \(m^2_{\text{simplex}}(\mathbf C)/
   m^2_{\text{simplex}}(\mathbf C')\) of the Paper 20 simplex mass term
   across two conductor-total sectors of the same row are manifestly
   dimensionless and need neither \(c\) nor \(\hbar\) to be stated.
   **Status: settled-negative** at the anchored definition. Paper 20
   Definition 2.1's leading-\(T^{(4)}\) coefficient is exactly zero on the
   carry/isolated-axis specifications on \(\mathbb Z/6\) (Corollary 6.3
   (T1); ledger item R, four-thread arithmetic root). The candidate's
   *form* (the ratio of \(T^{(4)}\) coefficients) is firewall-legal; its
   *content* — that the ratio is a non-trivial conductor-fixed pure number
   — fails on \(\mathbb Z/6\). The negative branch pre-claimed in the U′
   falsifier fires on this target.
2. **Compton-type closure of the program's own mass object (Paper 20 +
   item T′ composition, "where mass meets the quantum").** The Compton
   *wavelength* \(\bar\lambda_C=\hbar/(mc)\) is a *length* and is permanently
   out of scope — exactly as the metre/second value of \(c\) is — and is
   named here as the firewall trap so it cannot be smuggled back in under a
   plausible-sounding paraphrase. What is admissible is the same relation
   read as a *dimensionless closure identity*,
   \(mc\,\bar\lambda_C/\hbar=1\), with the trivial-1 case (the identity by
   construction) explicitly excluded as informationless: the content is
   whether the program's own mass object — the Paper 20 simplex-mass term —
   closes, in its \(c\)/\(\hbar\)-roles, to a *non-trivial* conductor-fixed
   pure number. Status: **[C, reduced]**, anchored-definition discipline of
   §11.4 binding (entry: Paper 20 Definition 2.1; Paper 18 §4 SLD/Bures for
   the well-posedness of the closure). The §11.3 surviving structural
   number \(1/2^Q\) is *not* this target — it is the alternative
   geometric-combinatoric pure number the same row furnishes, not the
   simplex-mass closure — and the two are not to be confused.
3. **The \(\alpha\)-shaped prime-reciprocal pure number (Paper 33 Q3 anchor;
   highest firewall risk).** The historically canonical scale-free
   \(c\)/\(\hbar\) number is the fine-structure constant
   \(\alpha=e^2/(4\pi\varepsilon_0\hbar c)\), a pure number combining a
   charge magnitude with \(c\) and \(\hbar\). The program has *no* measured
   charge primitive: its EM-sector content is the Cartan \(\mathfrak u(1)\)
   of Paper 14 and the **prime-reciprocal hypercharge weighting**
   \(Y=\tfrac12 P_2-\tfrac13 P_3\) of Paper 33 Q3. The admissible question
   is therefore strictly *structural*: does the prime-reciprocal
   combinatorics fix a pure number that plays the *structural role* \(\alpha\)
   plays for \(c\)/\(\hbar\)/charge? Status: **[C, reduced]**, *strictest*
   firewall discipline of §11.4 binding (no value of \(\alpha\), no charge
   magnitude, no electron mass is claimed or inferred; Paper 33 Q7's
   anchored-definition rule explicitly blocks promotion until the
   prime-reciprocal weighting is anchor-checked against Paper 33 §2).

Three *exclusions* recorded with the taxonomy (anti-traps):

- **No length, ever** — including no Compton wavelength, no electron mass,
  no \(\hbar\)-in-joules, no \(c\)-in-metres, no \(\alpha\)-value. The
  Compton wavelength is the most natural-seeming firewall trap of the pair
  and is named here so the editing discipline cannot drift across it.
- **Trivial-1 exclusion.** A combination that is dimensionless only because
  it is definitionally \(1\) (e.g. \(mc\bar\lambda_C/\hbar=1\) by
  construction) carries no content as a U′ deliverable and is not to be
  presented as an inferred constant.
- **No free non-combinatoric input.** A candidate counts only if it is forced
  by the row's conductor/cumulant combinatorics; a "dimensionless"
  combination that requires a measured input is not a program constant and
  is rejected on sight.

**Falsifier (U′, both branches pre-claimed; matched-pair discipline of K/L
and Paper 33 Q6).** If every scale-free combination of the \(c\)-role, the
\(\hbar\)-role, and the conductor/cumulant combinatorics is either
(a) trivially \(1\) by construction, or (b) dependent on a free
non-combinatoric input, then the \(c\)–\(\hbar\) pair fixes *no* non-trivial
inferable constant — the named pair of T′/\(c\) yields invariants but no
derived pure number — and U′ closes negative on the pair. Target 1 has
already fired this branch on \(\mathbb Z/6\); targets 2 and 3 remain open.
Conversely, a single non-trivial conductor-fixed pure number on either
remaining target *confirms* U′ and is itself a clean result. Targets 2 and
3 are not to be advanced past one revision of §12 without the anchored-
definition check of §11.4 against, respectively, Paper 20 Definition 2.1 /
Paper 18 §4 and Paper 33 Q3 / Q7.

#### 11.2.2 The firewall as theorem (T13 derivation) [structural elevation — added v0.2.5; ledger WW]

Until v0.2.5, the §11.2 firewall was stated as a **discipline rail**: the framework *chooses* not to claim dimensionful magnitudes ($G$, Planck length, $\alpha$, mass spectrum, $\hbar$ value, $c$ value, $\Lambda_{\mathrm{QCD}}$, cosmological scales), because the simplex carries no length/time/mass scale (Paper 20 §4) and because adjacent literature has crossed this boundary with smuggled inputs (e.g. $mc^2$, $\hbar/(mc)$). The choice was epistemically correct but its status was *methodological*: a self-imposed restraint.

T13 (Murillo Montero 2026, "Exact Simplicial Renormalization") changes the status of the firewall. We now state the theorem version:

**Firewall Theorem (T13-anchored).** *Let the categorical-simplex framework on $\mathbb Z/N$ be the finite arithmetic structure with: (a) the conductor lattice $\mathcal D_N=\{d\mid N:d>1\}$ as a finite poset; (b) the packet decomposition $H=\bigoplus_{d\in\mathcal D_N\cup\{1\}}H_d$; (c) the closure operator $\operatorname{Cl}_n:\mathcal P(\mathcal D_N)\to\mathcal P(\mathcal D_N)$ of T13 Theorem 9; (d) the apex closure polynomial $P_x\in\mathbb R[t]/(P_x)$ of T12 Theorem 6. Then every finite-RG-derived quantity of the framework is determined by (a)–(d), and none of (a)–(d) carries dimensionful information. Therefore no finite-RG-derived quantity of the framework can carry dimensionful information.*

**Proof.** By T13 Theorem 7 (Universality of Fusion Completion), the completed retained sector $H_{\operatorname{Cl}_n(S)}$ is independent of any choice of basis, coordinate projection, Helmert presentation, character representatives, or channel coordinates — it is determined by $(N,n,S)$ alone, i.e. by the finite lattice $\mathcal D_N$ and the integer interaction order. By T13 Theorem 9 (Fusion-Closure RG), the universality classes of the finite simplicial RG are exactly the fibers of $\operatorname{Cl}_n$ on $\mathcal P(\mathcal D_N)$. By T13 Theorem 6 (Renormalizability Criterion), the exactly renormalizable retained sectors are exactly the fusion-closed packet sets. By T13 Theorem 4 (Finite Renormalization Closure), every retained effective tower lives in the finite coordinate algebra $A_S=\mathbb R[z_1,\ldots,z_m]/I(Y_S(\Omega))$, generated by the *evaluation* of finitely many integer-indexed observables on the finite state set $\Omega$ — no real-valued metric scale, no continuous parameter, no infinitesimal quantity enters. By T12 Theorem 6 (Finite Apex Determinacy), the apex moment/cumulant tower closes inside $\mathbb R[t]/(P_x)$ where $P_x$ is a finite-degree polynomial whose roots are *rational linear combinations of integer ledger values* — no dimensionful scale is introduced at any moment level.

Each ingredient (a)–(d) is therefore a **finite combinatorial gadget** with no parameter carrying a physical unit. The map from $(\mathcal D_N,\operatorname{Cl}_n,P_x)$ to any derived quantity of the framework is dimension-preserving in the trivial sense: it sends "no dimensions" to "no dimensions." Therefore the image — every finite-RG-derived structural fact, every cumulant ratio, every coupling-orbit invariant, every closure polynomial root — is *dimensionless by construction*. $\square$

**Status elevation.**

| §11.2 statement | Pre-T13 (v0.2.4 and earlier) | Post-T13 (v0.2.5) |
|---|---|---|
| Why no dimensionful predictions? | Discipline (no smuggled inputs) | Theorem (closure operator on finite lattice cannot produce dimensionful output) |
| Tier of firewall | Methodological [A] | Mathematical [P], proved |
| What changes if the firewall were violated? | A self-imposed rule is broken | A theorem of T13 + T12 is violated, i.e. the framework's internal structure has been exited |

The firewall is no longer a *guard* against overreach. It is a *theorem about closure operators on finite combinatorial lattices*. To claim $G$, $\alpha$, or any mass, one must leave the closure-operator framework — at which point one is no longer in the categorical-simplex program but in some larger embedding which is *not* what T0–T13 build.

**Three structural consequences.**

(C1) **The framework is necessarily a *layer* in physics, not its totality.** Whatever the full theory of nature is, the categorical-simplex framework can at most be the *finite-arithmetic spine* of it. The dimensionful body — meters, seconds, kilograms, volts, scales — must live in a strictly larger structure that contains the spine but is not contained by it. The firewall is the *boundary* of that containment.

(C2) **No path inside T0–T13 reaches a dimensionful prediction.** The forward doors of T11 (RR catalog), the higher-order extensions of T12 (multivariate, noncommutative), and the renormalization-flow content of T13 (Schur, beta, closure-lattice) all remain inside the closure-operator framework and therefore inside the firewall. Door 5 of T11 (Newton-Hankel finite-rank, discharged by T12) is the deepest move available *inside* the closure-operator framework; even after this move, the firewall holds — by the theorem above.

(C3) **The only legitimate path to dimensionful content is the operator-algebraic completion (T13 §12.5 / T14 §10.2).** T13 §12.5 and T14 §10.2 both explicitly name the density-matrix / operator-algebra analog of finite renormalization as a next technical layer outside the present framework. Operator algebras carry modular Hamiltonians, which carry energy scales — *therefore* the operator-algebraic completion is the *only* known direction in which the framework's spine might legitimately acquire a dimensionful body. **This is the framework's matched-pair pre-claim:** either the operator-algebraic completion (prospectively a paper downstream of T14 in the lamed-series, *not* T14 itself — T14 is the geometric layer; the continuum problem is named as T15 in T14 §10.1; the operator-algebra completion lives in T14 §10.2 as a separate forward door, T15+ or Paper 50 in the numbered-paper series) introduces dimensionful content legitimately via modular flow, in which case the convergence-to-physics story changes; or the firewall theorem extends to the operator-algebra layer, in which case the framework is permanently the arithmetic spine. **Both branches are publishable, refereeable, and structurally well-posed.**

(C4) **The firewall theorem extends to curvature.** T14 Theorem 3 (Boundary Curvature) proves that the projected curvature defect $\mathcal R_S^{(n)}$ has universal support on the conductor-fusion boundary $\partial_n S\subseteq\mathcal D_N$ — a finite combinatorial lattice. By the same closure-operator argument above, no dimensionful curvature scale ($G$, Planck curvature, Ricci scalars in $\mathrm{km}^{-2}$, cosmological constant magnitudes) can be derived inside the framework. **The framework's gravity-as-curvature reading (§5 / §5.A / §5.B / item R′ Cor 9.10) is permanently dimensionless-internal**: it lives on the same lattice as ledger items GG (gravity localizes to multiplicative units), OO ($A_3$ trichotomy), QQ (T11 Projection-Closure), UU (T13 RG capstone), VV (Schur calculation at $\mathbb Z/6$), and XX/YY (T14 substrate + §3/§5 promotion). Six items, one lattice, all dimensionless. Newton's constant, like $\alpha$ and $\hbar$, remains permanently external by the Firewall Theorem.

**Discipline rails strengthened, not weakened.** The §11.4 carried-label discipline, the §11.1 anti-overclaim rails, and the matched-pair K/L/joint-on-disjoint discipline of §12 all *bind more tightly* under §11.2.2 than they did under §11.2 alone. A future claim of any dimensionful constant — $G$, $\alpha$, $m_e$, $H_0$, $\Lambda_{\mathrm{QCD}}$, generation count — by anyone reading this paper would now be *not only* a §11.2 firewall violation but a *direct contradiction of the Firewall Theorem above*. The discipline is now a theorem; the theorem is now the discipline.

**Slogan:** *The firewall is not a wall the framework chose not to climb. It is the edge of the lattice the framework is built on.*

Recorded as **ledger item WW** in §12.

### 11.3 Admissible \(Q\)-fixed structural numbers: the orthant fraction \(1/2^{Q}\)

The §11.2 template — *structural*, never *dimensionful* — admits one concrete \(Q\)-fixed pure number on the present row, alongside Corollary 9.7's \(c\equiv1\). It is stated here because the natural-seeming target it replaces is precisely a firewall trap that an earlier framing carried.

**Anchor and the dropped \(\Lambda\) analogy.** The Hellinger embedding (Paper 13, Definition 14.6A) is \(\Psi(p)_a=2\sqrt{p_a}\); its image \(\Sigma_R^+\) is a sector of a round sphere of radius **exactly \(2\), independently of \(Q=|R|\)** — the radius is the normalization constant in \(2\sqrt{p_a}\), not a row-dependent scale. Any framing along the lines of "a \(\Lambda\)-like \(Q\)-set Hellinger-sphere radius" is therefore *refuted at the anchored definition* and is dropped. This is the row-geometric analog of the Compton trap and of the Newton-constant trap: the most natural-seeming dimensionful candidate is precisely the firewall violation.

**The structural datum that survives.** What *is* \(Q\)-fixed in the same geometry is the *positive-orthant solid-angle fraction*. The positive orthant \(\Sigma_R^+\) is exactly one of the \(2^Q\) sign-octants of the round sphere, so
\[
\boxed{\;\text{orthant fraction}\;=\;\frac{1}{2^{Q}}\;}\qquad\big(=\tfrac{1}{64}\text{ for }R=\mathbb{Z}/6\big),
\]
an exact rational determined entirely by \(Q\), with no free input and not trivially \(1\). The cross-row ratio between \(\mathbb{Z}/6\) and \(\mathbb{Z}/30\) is \(2^{24}\). Both quantities pass §11.2: they are *structural* (the geometric fraction of the sphere the positive cone occupies), never the radius or any length.

**Bound (do-not-cut).** \(1/2^Q\) is a *geometric-combinatoric* datum — elementary \(2^{-Q}\) for \(Q\) sign-choices — and is *not* a cosmological constant, a vacuum-energy density, or any physical \(\Lambda\). The deliverable is exactly: the program has a \(Q\)-determined exactly-rational structural number, the projection-closure form of a conductor/\(Q\)-fixed pure number. No physical role is claimed; the \(\Lambda\) name is permanently dropped because it is the framing that invites the overclaim (§11.1).

**Coherence with the real-cone obstruction [A].** The same \(2^Q\) is the cardinality of the sign-octant set whose distinguished single member (the positive orthant) the real-cone-preservation condition of Paper 14 Theorem 2.2′ preserves — the obstruction that *forces* the Bures lift. The orthant fraction here and the obstruction's octant count are counting the same object: the sign-character group of \(H_R\). Audit obligation: confirm the two \(2^Q\)'s coincide as that group (a one-line bookkeeping check, finite, near-certain, not yet discharged).

### 11.4 The carried-label discipline (methodological commitment)

Two constants candidates have now been executed against their anchored definitions: the simplex-mass-ratio target on \(\mathbb{Z}/6\) (Paper 20 OQ1) and the \(Q\)-fixed Hellinger-sphere "radius". On execution both *labels* turned out to be specifications the cited internal definitions did not support — the carry/isolated-axis simplex masses are exactly zero on \(\mathbb{Z}/6\) (Corollary 6.3 (T1)), and the Hellinger radius is \(Q\)-independent by construction (Paper 13 Def 14.6A). Both items closed cleanly — one bounded-positive (\(1/2^Q\) survives in place of the carried radius), one stated-negative — but the pattern is a method-level signal: a constants candidate's narrative plausibility is not a substitute for its anchored content.

We therefore institute the rule, as a commitment of the editing discipline: **no constants candidate is promoted past one revision of the §12 ledger without an anchored-definition check against the cited internal paper.** Any later constants item — the Compton-type closure number and the \(\alpha\)-shaped prime-reciprocal number of the §11.2 three-target taxonomy in particular — must be anchored to its source object (Paper 20 Definition 2.1 / Paper 33 Q3 / Paper 18 §4) before its ledger entry is upgraded. This rule is binding; it is recorded as a methodological commitment, not as a result.

