- **YY. [P, proved geometric — added v0.2.5; §3 / §5 tier upgrade via T14] — Paper 32 §3 "closure defect" and §5 "cubic vertex = Amari–Chentsov, gravity = projection-closure defect" promoted from [A/P, structural] to [P, proved geometric] via T14 Theorem 2 + Theorem 3 + Theorem 6 (Equivalence).** *T14 (Murillo Montero 2026, "Projected Flatness and Curvature Linearization") proves that for a flat lifted connection on the apex/ledger algebra and a smooth projection $\Pi_S$ onto a retained packet sector, the projected curvature $R^{\Pi_S}=\Pi_S\,d\Pi_S\wedge d\Pi_S\,\Pi_S$ has universal support exactly on the conductor-fusion boundary $\partial_n S$.* **Application:** Paper 32 §3's "closure defect" = projected curvature defect $\mathcal R_S^{(n)}=(1-\Pi_S-\Pi_1)V_n|_{H_S^{\otimes n}}$ (T14 Thm 3); Paper 32 §5's "cubic vertex = gravity = projection-closure defect" = T14 Thm 2 + Thm 3 at $n=3, N=6, S=\{2,3\}, \partial_3=\{6\}$; Paper 32 §6.4 Theorem 6.2's gravity-adjacent residual = projected cubic curvature defect of $V=A_2\oplus A_3$ on M, channel basis $\{\{3,2,2\}\to\chi_1, \{3,4,4\}\to\chi_5\}$ (item VV). **The §5 gravity-as-projection-closure-defect reading is now [P, proved geometric].** **T14 Thm 6 (Equivalence) makes the deeper recognition explicit:** projected curvature, projection noncommutation, boundary leakage, renormalization source, Noether defect, and beta source are *one finite object* — the conductor-fusion boundary $\partial_n S$ — in six languages. Paper 32's "closure defect / cubic vertex / gravity-adjacent residual / RG-source / Noether defect" cluster is one identity. **Firewall preserved:** §11.2.2 / item WW's C4 strengthening (firewall extends to curvature): T14 Thm 3 places projected curvature on the finite combinatorial lattice $\mathcal D_N$; no dimensionful curvature scale (Newton's constant, Planck curvature, Ricci-scalar magnitudes) is supplied; item R′ (§9.7 Corollary 9.10) remains [C, reduced], T14 does not advance it. **Tier:** [P, proved geometric] for the §3 / §5 / §6.4 geometric reading; [forbidden, by WW] for any dimensionful curvature magnitude. **Slogan:** *Curvature is what flat closure looks like after a nonclosed projection.* (§3 Remark 3.4, §5.B, §10.6.7n fifth reading; paired with item XX.)

- **XX. [P, structural — added v0.2.5; T14 substrate, closes the geometry/curvature axis] — Projected Flatness and Curvature Linearization (T14) gives the fourth closed structural axis of the framework.** *T14 (Murillo Montero 2026, "Projected Flatness and Curvature Linearization") proves six structure theorems culminating in a 6-way equivalence theorem unifying curvature, projection noncommutation, boundary leakage, renormalization source, Noether defect, and beta source as the same finite object — the conductor-fusion boundary $\partial_n S$.* **T14's six theorems:** (1) **Linear Lift** — nonlinear simplex dynamics is the normalized shadow of linear multiplication/transport in the ledger/apex algebra ($p=\mathcal N(q)$, $\dot q = M_h q$ linear); (2) **Curvature as Projection-Commutator** — for flat lifted connection $\nabla$ and projection $\Pi$, $R^\Pi(X,Y)=\Pi(d\Pi\wedge d\Pi)\Pi$; (3) **Boundary Curvature** — for conductor-packet projections, curvature support is exactly $\partial_n S$, sharp; (4) **Schur Curvature Correction** — same Schur as T13 Thm 3, read as curvature renormalization with $Q^{\mathrm{eff}}_S=Q_{SS}-Q_{SB}Q_{BB}^{-1}Q_{BS}$; (5) **Cubic Noether Defect** — inherited cubic conservation laws persist on cubic-fusion-closed sectors; failure supported on $\partial_3 S$, individual laws may persist if their Noether covector annihilates the boundary; (6) **Curvature-Renormalization-Noether Equivalence (capstone)** — six conditions equivalent: (i) $S$ is $n$-fusion-closed; (ii) vertex closes on $H_S$; (iii) $\mathcal R_S^{(n)}=0$; (iv) no universal Schur/cumulant correction forced; (v) every inherited Noether identity persists; (vi) discrete beta source vanishes for every enlargement. **Central compression:** *curvature = projection noncommutation = boundary leakage = renormalization source = Noether defect = beta source.* **Application to Paper 32:** §3 / §5 tier upgrade to [P, proved geometric] (item YY); §10.6.7n / item VV acquires fifth reading (projected curvature, with two M-leakage channels as explicit curvature defect basis); §11.2.2 / item WW gains C4 (firewall extends to curvature); §10.6.7g / item PP's continuum-limit bridge changes from *absent* to *named-but-unbuilt* (T14 §10.1 names T15 as continuum problem); "lifting floor" methodology grounded as T14 Thm 1. **Four closed structural axes** (T11 + T12 + T13 + T14): T11 closes character/conductor axis; T12 closes order/tensor axis; T13 closes projection/RG axis; **T14 closes geometry/curvature axis**. Each axis identifies the same finite object $\partial_n S$ in a different language — one boundary, four axes, six readings. **Three new structural slogans:** (S4) projected flatness ⇔ retained sector fusion-closed; (S5) curvature is the boundary cost of seeing a flat apex algebra through a nonclosed projection; (S6) the geometry of a retained model is the cost of the projection by which it is seen. **Limitations (T14 §9):** not all curvature in mathematics is projection nonclosure (finite apex only); does not remove intrinsic geometry; does not make boundary defects numerically large (magnitude depends on coefficients/weights); not every Noether law fails when $S$ is nonclosed; does not replace T13; does not yet pass to continuum (T15 problem). **Tier:** [P, structural — T14 substrate]; [P, proved geometric] for the §3/§5 promotion (item YY). T14 substrate-level discharge of Paper 32's "closure defect / geometry / curvature" cluster as one identity. **Slogan:** *The geometry of a retained model is the cost of the projection by which it is seen.* (§2.5.6d; paired with item YY.)

- **WW. [P, proved — added v0.2.5; firewall promoted from discipline to theorem; C4 added via T14] — The Firewall Theorem (T13 + T14 anchored): no finite-RG-derived quantity of the framework can carry dimensionful information.** *Until v0.2.5 the §11.2 dimensional firewall was a discipline rail (the framework *chose* not to claim $G$, $\hbar$ magnitude, $c$ magnitude, $\alpha$, masses, scales). T13's closure-operator structure changes the firewall's status from methodological to mathematical.* **Theorem statement.** Let the categorical-simplex framework be the finite arithmetic structure with: (a) conductor lattice $\mathcal D_N$ as a finite poset; (b) packet decomposition $H=\bigoplus_{d\in\mathcal D_N\cup\{1\}}H_d$; (c) closure operator $\operatorname{Cl}_n:\mathcal P(\mathcal D_N)\to\mathcal P(\mathcal D_N)$ of T13 Thm 9; (d) apex closure polynomial $P_x$ of T12 Thm 6. Then every finite-RG-derived quantity is determined by (a)–(d), and none of (a)–(d) carries dimensionful information. **Therefore no finite-RG-derived quantity can carry dimensionful information.** **Proof sketch.** T13 Thm 7 (Universality of Fusion Completion): completed sector independent of coordinates. T13 Thm 9 (Fusion-Closure RG): universality classes = fibers of $\operatorname{Cl}_n$ on a finite lattice. T13 Thm 6: exactly renormalizable sectors = fusion-closed sets. T13 Thm 4: effective tower lives in $A_S=\mathbb R[z]/I(Y_S(\Omega))$ — evaluation of integer-indexed observables on finite $\Omega$, no continuous parameter. T12 Thm 6: apex tower closes in $\mathbb R[t]/(P_x)$ with rational-integer-combination roots. All four ingredients are finite combinatorial gadgets with no physical-unit parameter; the map to derived quantities sends "no dimensions" to "no dimensions." $\square$ **Status elevation:** the firewall went from [A, methodological] to [P, mathematical]. Pre-T13: violating it broke a self-imposed rule. Post-T13: violating it contradicts a T13 + T12 theorem, i.e. exits the framework. **Three structural consequences:** (C1) **the framework is necessarily a *layer* in physics, not its totality** — the dimensionful body must live in a strictly larger structure containing the spine but not contained by it; (C2) **no path inside T0–T13 reaches a dimensionful prediction** — every closure-operator move stays inside the firewall theorem; (C3) **the only legitimate path is the operator-algebraic completion (T13 §12.5 / T14 §10.2)** — modular Hamiltonians carry energy scales, and this is the only known direction the spine might acquire a dimensionful body; matched-pair K/L pre-claim opens on a paper downstream of T14 in the lamed-series (NOT T14 itself — T14 is the geometric layer; the operator-algebra completion lives at T14 §10.2 as a forward door, T15+ or Paper 50 in the numbered-paper series); K = operator-algebra layer introduces dimensionful content legitimately via modular flow; L = firewall theorem extends to operator-algebra layer; both publishable. **(C4) the firewall theorem extends to curvature** (T14 Thm 3 Boundary Curvature: projected curvature lives on $\partial_n S\subseteq\mathcal D_N$, a finite combinatorial lattice carrying no physical-unit parameter; the framework's gravity-as-curvature reading is permanently dimensionless-internal). **Discipline strengthening:** §11.4 carried-label, §11.1 anti-overclaim, matched-pair K/L all bind *more tightly* — any future claim of a dimensionful constant is now not only a §11.2 violation but a direct contradiction of the Firewall Theorem. **Slogan:** *The firewall is not a wall the framework chose not to climb. It is the edge of the lattice the framework is built on.* **Tier:** [P, proved] — derivation entirely inside T0–T13 substrate, uses no new mathematical content. Anchors the framework's permanent epistemic status as the arithmetic spine of physics, not its body. (§11.2.2)

- **VV. [P, computed — added v0.2.5; T13 Thm 3 execution at \(\mathbb Z/6\)] — Schur-complement effective vertex on $V=A_2\oplus A_3$: the renormalization-theoretic reading of Paper 47's V ⊥ M, with explicit identification of the two cubic boundary-source channels.** *T13 Theorem 3 (Schur Complement Renormalization) applied to the framework's natural quadratic kernel (Fisher–Rao at uniform centroid) on $\mathbb Z/6$ with $S=\{2,3\}, B=\{6\}$.* **Quadratic Schur calculation (explicit):** Fisher–Rao at centroid in real character basis $(c_3, c_2, s_2, c_1, s_1)$ ordered as $V\oplus M$ gives $g=6\cdot I_5$ with block structure $g_{VV}=6\cdot I_3$, $g_{MM}=6\cdot I_2$, $g_{VM}=g_{MV}=0$ (Pontryagin orthogonality of distinct-conductor characters). Therefore $Q^{\mathrm{eff}}_V = g_{VV}-g_{VM}g_{MM}^{-1}g_{MV} = 6\cdot I_3-0 = g_{VV}$. **The Schur complement is identically trivial.** **Interpretation:** this is the renormalization-theoretic dual of Paper 47's all-orders V ⊥ M result. Paper 47 (kinematic): V and M Hilbert-orthogonal at every order. T13 Thm 3 instance (dynamical/RG): therefore V is quadratically self-contained under boundary integration of M. Two layers of one fact: kinematic vs. dynamical. **First explicit renormalization-theoretic computation in the framework.** **Cubic content (where the action moves):** quadratic triviality means RG content is at cubic+. Channel-by-channel enumeration of $V_3(H_V,H_V,H_V)$ on character multisets in $\{2,3,4\}$ with output $\bmod 6$: 6 channels close in V ($\{3,3,3\}, \{3,3,2\}, \{3,3,4\}, \{3,2,4\}, \{2,2,4\}, \{2,4,4\}$), 2 channels leak to M ($\{3,2,2\}\to\chi_1$, $\{3,4,4\}\to\chi_5$), 2 close trivially ($\{2,2,2\}, \{4,4,4\}\to\chi_0$). **The two M-leakage channels are the explicit T13 Thm 1 boundary source.** Prime-structural content: each M-channel has one $A_2$ leg + two $A_3$ legs, output in $(\mathbb Z/6)^\times=\{1,5\}$ — explicit channel realization of ledger item GG "gravity localizes to multiplicative units." **Three T13 Thm 6 options at Z/6 cubic:** (i) adjoin M → fusion-closed $\{2,3,6\}$, exactly renormalizable (Paper 32 §6 full theory); (ii) integrate M out via Thm 2 → V-marginal exact, no induced correction at any order (Paper 47 V-effective in T13 language); (iii) truncate to V-closing channels, omit M → not fusion-closed, not exactly renormalizable — *this is Paper 32 §6.4 Theorem 6.2's gravity-adjacent residual structure in T13 language*. The omission of the two boundary-source channels IS the gravity-adjacent residual. **Discharges:** the renormalization-theoretic reading of Paper 47's audit $\delta$; the channel-level reading of Paper 32 §6.4 Theorem 6.2; the explicit content of T13 Thm 3 at the framework's natural quadratic kernel. **Connection to other ledger items:** GG (gravity localizes to $(\mathbb Z/6)^\times$) ↔ output indices $\{1,5\}$ of M-leakage channels; OO ($A_3$ trichotomy) ↔ retained-channel color classification; QQ (T11 Projection-Closure) ↔ $\partial_3\{2,3\}=\{6\}$ identity; UU (T13 RG capstone) ↔ the renormalization theorem on top. Five items, one structural fact, now read at four layers (kinematic, RG-quadratic, channel-cubic, multiplicative-arithmetic). **Tier:** [P, computed] — explicit finite linear-algebra calculation + explicit channel enumeration. **Slogan:** *V is quadratically closed and cubically leaking. The Schur theorem says the first half; the Boundary Source theorem names the second half. The framework's "gravity" is the deliberate omission of the second half.* (§10.6.7n)

- **UU. [P, structural — added v0.2.5; T13 substrate, closes the projection/RG axis] — Exact Simplicial Renormalization (T13) turns Paper 32 §6 into a finite renormalization theorem.** *T13 (Murillo Montero 2026, "Exact Simplicial Renormalization") proves nine structure theorems culminating in the finite-RG capstone: \(\mathbf{S\mapsto\operatorname{Cl}_n(S)}\) **is a closure operator on the finite packet lattice, whose fixed points are exactly the exactly renormalizable packet sectors.*** **T13's nine theorems:** (1) Boundary Source Decomposition — \(V_n=\Pi_SV_n+(1-\Pi_S)V_n\) with \((1-\Pi_S)V_n\subseteq\bigoplus_{d\in\partial_nS}H_d\) sharp; (2) Exact Boundary Integration — \(K_{\mathrm{eff},S}(J_S)=K(J_S,0)\), retained cumulants are full connected cumulants with retained external legs, no approximation; (3) Schur Complement Renormalization — quadratic effective kernel \(Q^{\mathrm{eff}}_S=Q_{SS}-Q_{SB}Q_{BB}^{-1}Q_{BS}\) exact; (4) Finite Renormalization Closure — retained effective tower lives in finite coordinate algebra \(A_S=\mathbb R[z]/I(Y_S(\Omega))\) with diagonal closure polynomial \(P_{S,h}\); (5) Beta Function as Boundary Curvature — \(\beta^{(n)}_{S\to S'}=0\iff\partial_nS\cap(S'\setminus S)=\varnothing\); at maximal target, \(\beta=0\) ⇔ \(S\) fusion-closed; (6) Renormalizability Criterion — \(H_S\) exactly renormalizable iff \(S\) is \(n\)-fusion-closed; minimal completion is \(H_{\operatorname{Cl}_n(S)}\); (7) Universality of Completion — \(H_{\operatorname{Cl}_n(S)}\) coordinate-independent; (8) Exact \(N=6\) Four-Sector Renormalization — on \(\mathbb Z/6\), \(\partial_3\{2,3\}=\{6\}\), cubic boundary forced; (9) Fusion-Closure RG (capstone) — \(\operatorname{Cl}_n\) is an extensive/monotone/idempotent closure operator on \(\mathcal P(\mathcal D_N)\); universality classes are fibers of \(\operatorname{Cl}_n\); discrete boundary-adjunction flow terminates at \(\operatorname{Cl}_n(S_0)\). **Central compression:** RG flow = boundary adjunction, fixed points = fusion-closed sectors. **Application to Paper 32:** §6 Theorem 6.2 (gravity-adjacent residual = M packet) IS the \(N=6, n=3, S=\{2,3\}\) instance of T13 Theorem 8 — promoted from finite Fourier calculation to finite renormalization theorem; Paper 47 V/M at Z/30 is now the unique RG-fixed-point sector at Z/30 cubic (V = retained, M = the cubic boundary source); §10.6.7j 5 fusion-closed sectors are the lattice of cubic RG-fixed points; §10.6.7k universal all-order leakage \(\partial_n V=\{6\}\) reads as "M is the universal RG-boundary of V at all orders"; §3 categorical effective action is the cumulant generating functional whose sectors T13 projects, with finite-data effective tower (T13 Thm 4 matches T12). **Three new structural slogans:** (S1) projected finite apex theory exactly renormalizable iff retained set fusion-closed; (S2) couplings run exactly when projection crosses a conductor-fusion boundary; (S3) finite RG = closure operator generated by conductor fusion. **Combined T11+T12+T13 picture (three closed axes):** T11 closes character/conductor axis (vertex calculus); T12 closes order/tensor axis (Hankel recurrence); **T13 closes projection/RG axis (closure operator)**. Framework has no algebraically free DOF beyond: (i) conductor lattice \(\mathcal D_N\); (ii) packet decomposition; (iii) closure operator \(\operatorname{Cl}_n\); (iv) apex closure polynomial \(P_x\). **Limitations (T13 §11):** not continuum Wilsonian QFT (reinforces item PP's Yang–Mills negative-bounding by 5 bridge-failures); not all residuals physical forces (Unification Thesis HH stays [A, structural]); doesn't replace T12; doesn't imply every projection should be closed — Paper 32's gravity-adjacent residual is *deliberately omitted M*, T13 quantifies the price of this exclusion via Thm 2. **Tier:** [P, structural] — T13 substrate-level discharge of Paper 32's "projection-residual / RG-flow" reading. No tier upgrades on §6 or §10.6 results; the discharge is at the level of *why* the framework's projection is exactly renormalization-theoretic at finite arithmetic. **Slogan:** *projection does not create arbitrary error; it creates a boundary source*. (§2.5.6c)

- **TT. [P, structural — added v0.2.5; discharges RR forward door 8] — The Finite Apex Determinacy Theorem (T12) closes the order/tensor axis of Paper 32's framework.** *T12 (Murillo Montero 2026, "The Finite Apex Determinacy Theorem") proves six structure theorems culminating in the finite-algebraic compression \(\text{apex tower} \cong \mathbb R[t]/(P_x)\), where \(P_x(t) = \prod_{j=1}^r (t - \lambda_j)\) and \(\lambda_j\) are the distinct values of the centered ledger.* **T12's six theorems:** (1) Finite Spectral Support: \(\mu_n = \sum_j W_j \lambda_j^n\); (2) Hankel Rank Closure: rank\(H_k = \min(k+1, r)\) with degree-\(r\) recurrence; (3) Newton-Hankel Reconstruction: finite prefix \(\mu_0, \ldots, \mu_{2r-1}\) determines \(P_x\), levels, weights; (4) Channel-Resolved Closure: every Fourier channel obeys SAME closure polynomial; (5) Cumulant Closure: cumulants generated by finite spectral data; (6) Finite Apex Determinacy: apex tower \(\cong \mathbb R[t]/(P_x)\). **Application to Paper 32:** §3's "infinite cumulant tower" is replaced by the finite quotient algebra \(\mathbb R[t]/(P_x)\); §10.6.7m's connected quartic \(\kappa_4 = \mu_4 - 3\mu_2^2\) is finitely determined; §10.6.7k's universal all-order leakage support is order-axis finite-rank; each character channel \(\mathcal M_x(\beta, c)\) obeys the same degree-\(r\) recurrence (T12 Thm 4). **At Z/6:** uniform centroid \(r=1\) (scalar tower trivial); generic point \(r=6\) (at most 6 independent moments); symmetric 2+2+2 \(r=3\) (T12 §8 worked example matches Paper 32 §6.2A pattern). **Strengthens Paper 22 RH-bridge:** all-order Noether-Weil positivity is finite-data (finitely many cumulants suffice). **Strengthens Paper 47 audit δ:** all-orders V ⊥ M decoupling is finite-rank verification; orders \(m > r\) forced by recurrence. **Combined T11 + T12 picture:** T11 closes character/conductor axis (vertex calculus); T12 closes order/tensor axis (Hankel recurrence); framework is totally finite arithmetic perturbation theory with no algebraically free degrees of freedom beyond a finite combinatorial structure. **Limitations (T12 §10):** scalar only (multivariate is T12 §11.3 forward door); commutative only (Bures noncommutative is T12 §11.5 forward door); doesn't replace T11. **Tier:** [P, structural] — T12 substrate-level discharge of Paper 32's "infinite tower" framing. No tier upgrades on §6 or §10.6 results; the discharge is at the level of *why* the framework's order-tower is closed (finite quotient algebra) rather than *whether* the results hold. Slogan: *higher order is real, but not freely new*. (§2.5.6b)

- **SS. [P, computed — added v0.2.5; executes T11 forward doors 1, 2, 3, 5, 10 + structural door 4] — Six new subsections §§10.6.7h–m promoted from RR forward-door notes to full Paper 32 content with derivations.** *Six structurally important results now have full Paper 32 subsections instead of forward-door-note status:* **§10.6.7h: Quartic vertex enumeration on Z/6 — 12 closing tuples** (full packet classification; all three packets $A_2$, $A_3$, $M$ have pure quartic self-closures, ratio 1:1:1 in cubic-vertex weight). **§10.6.7i: Order-specificity of Cor 6.1d.2** — $A_2$ is cubically isolated but quartically self-coupling (pure-$A_2$ quartic vertex $\{3,3,3,3\}$ closes via T11 Thm 3.1 at $p=2, m=4$ even allowing cancellation; the cubic obstruction at $p=2, m=3$ odd is overcome at quartic). **§10.6.7j: Fusion-closed sub-theories at Z/6 cubic** — complete classification of 5 fusion-closed sectors $\emptyset, \{A_2\}, \{A_3\}, \{A_2,M\}, \{A_2,A_3,M\}$ forming a meet-semilattice; the new closed sector $\{A_2, M\}$ (parity + gravity-adjacent without color) is structurally accessible but was not in Paper 32 v0.2.4. **§10.6.7k: Universal all-order leakage support** — $\partial_n V = \{6\}$ for ALL $n \ge 3$ at Z/6 (proof via T11 Thm 4.1 + explicit Fuse calculations at $n=4$); M-packet is *universal* leakage support across all orders, not merely cubic residual; strengthens Paper 32 §13.1 depth audit from depth-axis to order-axis. **§10.6.7l: Z/30 V/M is forced cubic-completion** — explicit computation $\operatorname{Cl}_3(\{2,3,5\}) = \{2,3,5,6,10,15,30\}$ = entire non-trivial divisor lattice; Paper 47's V/M decomposition is now a *theorem-level consequence* of T11 Cor 5.2 minimal fusion completion, not a row-specific structural choice. **§10.6.7m: Connected-diagram interpretation of $T^{(4)}$** — $\kappa_4 = \mu_4 - 3\mu_2^2$ via Möbius inversion makes Paper 20's simplex-mass term *structurally* the first connected quartic vertex (T11 Cor 2.2 "birth of closure defect"); discharges Paper 32 §3 promissory note on the structural meaning of "closure defect". **Tier:** [P, computed] for §§10.6.7h, i, j, k, l (five computational sections); [A, structural] for §10.6.7m (connected-diagram interpretation). **Discharges 6 of 10 RR forward doors immediately:** doors 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 10. Remaining 4 (Helmert verification, bilateral additive+multiplicative, Newton-Hankel finite-rank, higher-order cascade) recorded as continuing forward doors. **Most important new content:** §10.6.7i's order-specificity of $A_2$ isolation reveals a *new analytical dimension* (the order-axis / depth of closure tower) within fixed-row analysis, complementary to the primorial-axis (Z/6 → Z/30) and depth-axis (Z/6 → Z/12) dimensions Paper 32 already exploits. (§§10.6.7h–m)

- **RR. [P, computed (4 entries) + forward doors (6 entries) — added v0.2.5] — Forward doors from T11: what Paper 32 and Paper 47 have NOT yet exploited.** *T11 opens ten structural forward doors, four of which are immediate [P, computed] discoveries available to v0.2.5; the remaining six are explicitly-named forward-door obligations.* **Immediate [P, computed] new structural facts:** (i) **Pure-\(A_2\) quartic self-closure** \(\{3,3,3,3\}\) (sum 12 ≡ 0 mod 6) ⇒ Cor 6.1d.2's "A_2 cubic isolation" is **order-specific** — \(A_2\) is cubically isolated but **quartically self-coupling**. New structural statement Paper 32 has not articulated. (ii) **Paper 47's V/M decomposition at Z/30 is the FORCED cubic-completion**: \(\operatorname{Cl}_3(\{2,3,5\})=\{2,3,5,6,10,15,30\}\) = entire non-trivial divisor lattice. The V/M split is the minimal forced extension by T11 Cor 5.2, not a choice. (iii) **5 fusion-closed sectors at Z/6 cubic** (not 2): \(\{\emptyset, \{2\}, \{3\}, \{2,6\}, \{2,3,6\}\}\). The sector \(\{2,6\}=A_2\oplus M\) — parity + gravity-adjacent without color — is fusion-closed; Paper 32 has not considered this sub-theory. (v) **Universal leakage support** \(\partial_n V=\{6\}\) for all \(n\ge 3\) at Z/6: **M is the all-order leakage support of V, not merely the cubic residual.** Cor 6.1d.2 is order-specific; the M-localization is order-universal. **Forward doors (named but not executed):** (iv) Connected-diagram \(T^{(4)}\) = simplex-mass = connected quartic vertex (T11 Cor 2.2); (vi) Helmert-basis verification of cubic structure constant via T9's transfer matrix (T11 §9.3); (vii) Bilateral additive + multiplicative vertex calculus combining T11 + T8 (T11 §7); (viii) Newton-Hankel finite-rank closure — at Z/N only N independent cumulants (T11 §9.4 / T12 forecast); (ix) Higher-order fusion completion cascade at Z/30, Z/210, ...; (x) Full quartic-vertex packet classification on Z/6 (12 closing tuples, all three packets having pure quartic self-closures). **Tier:** [P, computed] for doors 1, 2, 3, 5 (immediate v0.2.5 discoveries); [A, structural] for door 4 (connected-diagram interpretation, requires Möbius computation); [forward door] for doors 6, 7, 8, 9, 10 (not executed). **Significance:** door 1 (\(A_2\) quartic self-closure) is the most structurally important — it reveals that the framework's "isolation" is order-specific and that depth-2 of the closure tower brings new structural content (an "EW-depth-like" effect *within* a fixed row, distinct from the EW-depth Z/12 result of §10.6.7c). Door 2 (Z/30 V/M forcing) discharges Paper 47's V/M as a theorem-level consequence, not a row-specific choice. (§2.5.7)

- **QQ. [P, structural — added v0.2.5] — The Apex Vertex Calculus (T11) discharges Paper 32 §6 as a worked example of a general theorem.** *T11 (Murillo Montero 2026, "The Apex Vertex Calculus") proves three structure theorems that subsume Paper 32 §6's central calculations as special cases.* **T11 §2 Theorem 2.1 (Apex Feynman Rule):** every Taylor coefficient and every integer closure sample of the apex generator is computed by finite character-conservation \(n\)-leg vertices \(V_n(a_1,\ldots,a_n;c)=\mathbf 1[a_1+\cdots+a_n\equiv c\pmod N]\); generalizes Paper 32 Lemma 6.1a from \(n=3,N=6\) to all \(n\) and all \(N\). **T11 §3 Theorem 3.1 (Conductor Fusion Theorem):** packet products decompose prime-locally by \(p\)-adic cancellation rules with the odd-prime / \(p=2\)-odd-multiplicity / \(p=2\)-even-multiplicity trichotomy; Paper 32 Cor 6.1d.1 (\(A_3\) self-closure) is the odd-prime \(p=3, m=3\) case, and Cor 6.1d.2 (pure-\(A_2\) cubic vacuity) is the \(p=2, m=3\) odd-multiplicity case (no cancellation at prime 2). **T11 §4 Theorem 4.1 (Projection-Closure Theorem):** projected sector closure ⇔ fusion closure; the universal residual support is the **conductor-fusion boundary** \(\partial_n S\). **Paper 32 Theorem 6.2 (gravity-adjacent residual = \(M\) packet) is the \(N=6, n=3, S=\{2,3\}\) instance of T11 Theorem 4.1**, with \(\partial_3\{2,3\}=\{6\}\) exactly. **T11 §5 Cor 5.2 (Minimal Fusion Completion):** if a sector leaks, the smallest extension that closes is iterated fusion completion \(\operatorname{Cl}_n(S)\) — for Paper 32's \(\mathbb Z/6\): \(\operatorname{Cl}_3(\{2,3\})=\{2,3,6\}\), so adding \(M=H_6\) is the **forced minimal extension**, not an ad hoc addition. **T11 §6 worked example at \(N=6\)** reproduces Paper 32 Theorem 6.2 verbatim. **T11 §7 multiplicative parallel** gives the additive-multiplicative bridge underlying §2.5.4 / GG (gravity localizes to \((\mathbb Z/P_k)^\times\)). **Discharges:** §10.6.7f \(A_3\) color confinement trichotomy (the three classes are the three fusion-types of \(A_3\)-leg cubic vertices, all closing to conductor 1); §10.6.7c depth rows (fusion boundaries on Z/12, Z/18 add prime-power-depth packets); §10.6.7g YM negative assessment (T11 is finite-arithmetic perturbation theory, not continuum YM construction). **Slogan inherited from T11:** *every projected simplex theory leaks exactly through its conductor-fusion boundary*. **Tier:** [P, structural] — T11's theorems are finite combinatorial / Fourier-analytic statements; Paper 32 §6's [P] results inherit a structurally-universal proof framework. No tier upgrades; the framework was already at [P] on Z/6; T11 makes the [P] *structurally universal* at every \((N, n)\). (§2.5.6)

- **PP. [A, structural — added v0.2.5; NEGATIVE assessment with strict scope boundary] — Yang–Mills Existence and Mass Gap (Clay Millennium): structural shadows, NOT solution.** *The framework is **not approaching** the Clay-Millennium Yang–Mills Existence and Mass Gap problem. This negative-bounding is itself a Paper 32 deliverable to prevent overclaim.* **Clay problem requirements (none satisfied by framework):** (1) measure on continuous connection space \(\mathcal A(\mathbb R^4)/\mathcal G\) satisfying Osterwalder–Schrader axioms; (2) spectral mass gap \(\Delta>0\); (3) continuum limit from any regularization with asymptotic freedom and confinement. **Framework status:** finite-arithmetic on \(\mathbb Z/N\), Bures lifts on \(\mathbb C^N\); NO continuous QFT, NO OS axioms, NO spectral gap (only \(m^2\ge 0\) inequality), NO continuum limit, NO Wilson-loop machinery, NO RG running. The framework is in the **NCG-lineage** (Connes–Chamseddine spectral triples) NOT the **constructive-QFT-lineage** (Glimm–Jaffe-style measures on infinite-dimensional spaces). **What the framework DOES have on YM axis (positive contributions, all structural-shadow only):** (F1) §10.6.7f color confinement signature at Z/6 — finite-arithmetic shadow; (F2) Paper 20 mass non-tachyonicity \(m^2_{\text{simplex}}\ge 0\) — inequality, not gap; (F3) §10.6.7b three-gauge trace unification on \(F_{30}\); (F4) Paper 18 §6 Bures-positivity + Petz monotonicity; (F5) Paper 32 §7 / Paper 22 Weil-positivity ↔ non-tachyonicity bridge (RH-shaped, also Clay); (F6) Paper 46 / §13.2B Hartle–Hawking signature with quartic positivity. **Five bridges to Clay solution, ALL absent:** continuum-limit construction, OS-axiom verification, spectral-gap upgrade, Wilson-loop area-law, asymptotic-freedom RG analysis. **T14 update (added v0.2.5):** the continuum-limit bridge is now **named** as the T15 problem (T14 §10.1: "directed systems of finite apex algebras and the question when projected curvature defects converge to smooth curvature tensors"), but **not built** — T15 is not written, and even when written, it would only address the continuum-curvature bridge, not the OS-axiom / spectral-gap / Wilson-loop / asymptotic-freedom bridges. Status of the five bridges: 1 named-but-unbuilt (continuum), 4 absent. **The Clay-YM-solver assessment remains NEGATIVE.** The change is structural-shape only: there is now a named next step in the direction continuum construction would need, where v0.2.4 had none. **Tier:** [A, structural] for the negative assessment; [P, computed] for framework's positive structural shadows; [forbidden] for any positive contribution to the Clay solution per se. **Discipline (binding):** §11.1 anti-overclaim positions the framework against the Clay-YM-solver register; §11.2 firewall blocks dimensionful magnitudes (no \(\Lambda_{QCD}\), no spectral gap in GeV, no string tension); the framework's "approaching Clay YM" claim — if anyone ever makes it — would be a **guardrail violation by 5 bridge-failures**. The framework provides structural-shadow content on the YM axis at identical-status epistemic level to its QG-shadow content (§10.5 Unification Thesis): genuine, articulate, firewall-protected. (§10.6.7g)

- **OO. [P, computed; QCD-confinement structural match — added v0.2.5] — Color confinement signature: the \(A_3\) trichotomy via the \(\mathbb Z/3\) deck at \((N=6, m=2)\).** *The \(\mathbb Z/3\) Kummer-cover deck at the Born/amplitude gauge on Z/6 sectorizes characters by \(c\bmod 3\) into three color sectors:* \(\rho_0=\{\chi_0,\chi_3\}\) (singlet, contains \(A_2\)); \(\rho_1=\{\chi_1,\chi_4\}\); \(\rho_2=\{\chi_2,\chi_5\}\). \(A_3=\{\chi_2,\chi_4\}\) fills the two non-trivial color sectors with one character each — **zero singlet content, "colored doublet"**. **\(A_3\) trichotomy of cubic vertices (computed by exhaustive enumeration of closing triples):** Type (i) **pure-\(A_3\) monochromatic** \(\{2,2,2\},\{4,4,4\}\) — 2 triples, \(d^{abc}\)-symmetric / cyclic-color / glueball-like; Type (ii) **\(A_3\) + monochromatic \(M\)-pair** \(\{1,1,4\},\{2,5,5\}\) — 2 triples, meson-like (\(q\bar q\) singlet with \(M\)-mediation); Type (iii) **tricolor \(A_3+A_2+M\)** \(\{1,2,3\},\{3,4,5\}\) — 2 triples, \(\epsilon^{abc}\)-antisymmetric / baryon-like (\(qqq\) singlet). **Total**: 2+2+2 = 6 triples, all closing triples involving \(A_3\). **Cubic-vertex weights (Lemma 6.1a universal \(T_{klm}=216\)):** each class contributes \(2\cdot 216 = 432\); ratio (i):(ii):(iii) **= 1:1:1 exact** on \(\mathbb Z/6\) centroid. **Pure-singlet cubic vacuity**: class (a) \((0,0,0)\) requires \(\{\chi_3,\chi_3,\chi_3\}\) with sum \(9\not\equiv 0\pmod 6\), so ZERO triples — this is Cor 6.1d.2's \(A_2\) isolation read as **color-singlet sector having no cubic self-coupling** (consistent with QCD pure-singlet cubic vacuity). **Two disambiguated senses of "isolation":** Sense 1 (Cor 6.1d.2): \(A_2\) is *completely cubically isolated* (no self-coupling, only cross-prime mediation) — inert-axis. Sense 2 (this section, Cor 6.1d.1 refined): \(A_3\) is *confinement-isolated* (couples freely, but only into color-singlets via 3 trichotomy classes) — confined-gauge-sector. **QCD confinement structural match:** baryon ↔ Type (iii), meson ↔ Type (ii), \(d^{abc}\) gluon vertex ↔ Type (i), all in color-singlet by \(\mathbb Z/3\) selection rule; no free colored states (\(A_3\cap\rho_0=\emptyset\)). **The framework's cubic Amari–Chentsov vertex on \(\mathbb Z/6\) encodes color confinement as a structural property of the conductor lattice.** **Tier:** [P, computed] for trichotomy enumeration and equal-weight result; [A, structural] for QCD-confinement mapping; [C, reduced] for specific coupling-strength predictions beyond the 1:1:1 ratio. (§10.6.7f)

- **NN. [A, structural — added v0.2.5] — String-theory structural connections.** *The framework structurally cohabits with string theory at specific algebraic levels, without being string theory itself.* **STRONG connections:** (A) Bott periodicity \(\mathbb Z/8\) at Z/24 cubic gauge ↔ KO-theory D-brane charge classification (Witten 1998; Minasian–Moore 1997) — same algebraic \(\mathbb Z/8\); (B) Kummer-cover deck groups \(\mu_N/\mu_{\gcd(N,m)}\) ↔ orbifold compactification quotients — same cyclic-group quotient structure; (C) Connes–Chamseddine NCG-SM ↔ string-theoretic SM derivations (heterotic, F-theory, intersecting branes) — parallel programs in the unification-beyond-SM literature; (G) \(\Lambda^2 E\oplus E^*=\mathbf{10}\oplus\bar{\mathbf 5}\) of SU(5) — identical fermion content per generation as string-theoretic SU(5) GUTs. **MODERATE:** (F) Z/30 SU(5) GUT structure ↔ string-theoretic SU(5) compactifications. **WEAK-shape:** (D) T5 reciprocal closure ↔ T-duality (\(R\leftrightarrow 1/R\)); (E) tropical limit of gauge corridor ↔ Maslov dequantization in tropical mirror symmetry. **The framework does NOT have**: worldsheets, critical dimensions 10/11/26, supersymmetry, Calabi–Yau / G2 / Kähler manifolds, string coupling, moduli stabilization, strings/branes as fundamental objects, the string-theoretic landscape. **The framework IS:** the NCG-lineage arithmetic cousin of string-theoretic SM unification, sharing algebraic-skeleton structures but not continuous-geometric content. **New matched-pair (K = arithmetic alternative; L = parallel cousins only; joint-on-disjoint = partial algebraic-level match):** pre-claimed; none asserted. **Tier:** [A] structural for A, B, F; [P] structural for C, G; [C] shape for D, E. **Firewall preserved equivalently:** the §11.2 firewall on dimensionful magnitudes binds in both programs (no string scale, no \(\alpha'\), no compactification radii, no Kaluza–Klein masses). (§10.6.7e)

- **MM. [P, computed + structural Bott link — added v0.2.5] — Going to \(\mathbb Z/24\): the deeper electroweak-depth row.** *Extension to depth-3 on prime 2: \(\mathbb Z/24=\mathbb Z/(2^3\cdot 3)=\mathbb Z/8\times\mathbb Z/3\).* **Setup unchanged from Z/6:** \(E_{24}=E_6=\mathbb C^2\oplus\mathbb C^3\), \(F_{24}=F_6\) dim 15, \(Y=(1/2)P_2-(1/3)P_3\) ⇒ \(\sin^2\theta_W^{\text{tree}}=3/8\). **New packet vs Z/12:** \(H_8\) (conductor 8, dim 4). **Conductor packets:** \(H_2, H_3, H_4, H_6, H_8, H_{12}, H_{24}\) with \(\varphi\)-values \((1, 2, 2, 2, 4, 4, 8)\). **Multiplicative-unit structure:** \((\mathbb Z/24)^\times=(\mathbb Z/2)^3\) — three independent parities, unique among small rows; compare Z/6 (\(\mathbb Z/2\)), Z/12 (\((\mathbb Z/2)^2\)), Z/18 (\(\mathbb Z/6\) cyclic), Z/30 (\(\mathbb Z/2\times\mathbb Z/4\)). **Kummer-cover deck groups at integer gauges:** SM gauge-center \(\mathbb Z/6\) appears at \(m=N/6=4\) (quartic gauge); color \(\mathbb Z/3\) at \(m=N/3=8\); chirality \(\mathbb Z/2\) at \(m=N/2=12\) (scaling law confirmed). **Striking new content:** the **cubic gauge \(m=3\) has Kummer-cover deck \(\mathbb Z/8\)** = the *Bott-periodicity period* of real K-theory, the same \(\mathbb Z/8\) that classifies KO-dimensions in spectral-triple theory. **The Connes–Chamseddine SM spectral triple uses KO-dim 6 (mod 8)** — selected by Connes–Chamseddine to give correct chirality / J / DJ structure of SM fermions. **Structural identification (Bott-KO match, new matched-pair, analogous to Face E §10.5.4):** *the Z/24 cubic-gauge \(\mathbb Z/8\) IS the framework's natural locus for the KO-dim assignment, with the SM choice "KO-dim = 6" selected by deck-element data*. K/L/joint-on-disjoint pre-claimed: K = identification holds (framework determines KO-dim 6 for SM); L = \(\mathbb Z/8\) coincidence only, no Bott-KO match; joint-on-disjoint = partial identification (\(\mathbb Z/8\) constrains but does not uniquely select KO-dim 6). **Physical-interpretation candidates (all [C, reduced]):** 2HDM / extended Higgs (depth-3 SU(2) sector); CP violation in EW (cubic-gauge Z/8 phase structure); KO-dim 6 specifier (Bott-KO match); Z/8 anomaly of time-reversal-invariant topological fermion phases (Witten 2016). **Three structural ladders identified:** depth-on-2 ladder Z/6→Z/12→**Z/24**→Z/48→... (EW depth); depth-on-3 ladder Z/6→Z/18→Z/54→... (QCD depth); prime-extension ladder Z/6→Z/30→Z/210→... (gauge enrichment). **Tier:** [P, computed] for traces, Kummer-decks, unit-structure, scaling-law; [A, structural] for Bott-KO identification; [C, reduced] for physical-interpretation candidates. (§10.6.7d)

- **LL. [P, computed — added v0.2.5] — Going to \(\mathbb Z/12\) and \(\mathbb Z/18\): the depth rows.** *Extension to the non-squarefree primorials \(\mathbb Z/12=\mathbb Z/(2^2\cdot 3)\) and \(\mathbb Z/18=\mathbb Z/(2\cdot 3^2)\) — same primes as Z/6 with prime-power depth.* **Setup unchanged from Z/6**: \(E_{12}=E_{18}=\mathbb C^2\oplus\mathbb C^3=E_6\), \(F=\Lambda^2 E\oplus E^*\) dim 15, \(Y=\tfrac{1}{2}P_2-\tfrac{1}{3}P_3\), giving \(\sin^2\theta_W^{\text{tree}}=3/8\) **invariant under prime-power depth**. **New content vs Z/6:** prime-power-depth packets \(H_4\) at Z/12 (\(\varphi(4)=2\)) and \(H_9\) at Z/18 (\(\varphi(9)=6\)). **Kummer-cover deck-group scaling law (derived):** for every \(N\) divisible by 6, the SM gauge-center \(\mathbb Z/6=\mathbb Z/3\times\mathbb Z/2\) appears at gauge rung \(m=N/6\); color \(\mathbb Z/3\) at \(m=N/3\); chirality \(\mathbb Z/2\) at \(m=N/2\). Verified at Z/6 (\(m=1,2,3\)), Z/12 (\(m=2,4,6\)), Z/18 (\(m=3,6,9\)), Z/30 (\(m=5,10,15\)). **Physical interpretation (structural):** Z/12 = electroweak-depth row (\(H_4\) carries the Higgs / SU(2)-symmetry-breaking content); Z/18 = QCD-depth row (\(H_9\) carries the chiral-symmetry-breaking / confinement content). **Primorial-and-depth hierarchy:** Z/6 (SM gauge skeleton) < Z/12 (EW-depth) < Z/18 (QCD-depth) < Z/30 (GUT). **Confirmed by Paper 47 §8.4 audit χ:** binary V/M K-branch holds at Z/12 (V ⊥ M at machine floor); trichotomy V/W/M with W=\(H_4\) gives **joint-on-disjoint** (W ⊥ M overlap 0.447, NOT machine floor) — interpreted as Higgs-gravity mixing at higher orders. **Subtlety:** the framework's structural ordering Z/12 < Z/18 (by \(N\)) does NOT match the physical energy ordering (QCD ~ 1 GeV < EW ~ 100 GeV); the framework predicts that EW-depth and QCD-depth rows *exist* but the EW/QCD assignment is phenomenological, not framework-derivable (firewall on numerical scales). **Tier:** [P, computed] for traces and scaling law; [A, structural] for the EW/QCD assignment. (§10.6.7c)

- **KK. [P, computed — added v0.2.5] — Going to \(\mathbb Z/30\): the GUT-scale row.** *Extension of the §10.6.1 calculation to the next squarefree primorial \(\mathbb Z/30=\mathbb Z/(2\cdot 3\cdot 5)\), with spectral-triple inner Hilbert space \(E_{30}=\mathbb C^2\oplus\mathbb C^3\oplus\mathbb C^5\) (dim 10) and fermion module \(F_{30}=\Lambda^2 E_{30}\oplus E_{30}^*\) (dim 55, NOT \(3\times 15\) of three SM generations).* **Trace calculations:** \(\mathrm{Tr}(Y^2)|_{F_{30}}=15/2\), \(\mathrm{Tr}(T_a^2)|_{F_{30}}=9/2\) for each of \(a\in\{SU(2), SU(3), SU(5)\}\) — *automatic three-way trace coincidence*, the categorical-simplex three-gauge unification condition realized on \(F_{30}\). **Tree Weinberg-like angles:** \(\sin^2\theta^{(a)}|_{\text{tree}}=T_a/(T_a+T_Y)=(9/2)/(12)=3/8\) for all three gauge factors against \(U(1)_Y\) — same 3/8 as Z/6 (§10.6.1), preserved across the primorial extension. **Fermion content of Z/30 contains the SU(5)-GUT 15-fermion content per generation:** the SU(5) decuplet \((\mathbf 1,\mathbf 1,\mathbf{10})\) (dim 10) plus the antifundamental \((\mathbf 1,\mathbf 1,\bar{\mathbf 5})\) (dim 5) — together 15 dim, precisely the SU(5)-GUT fermion content of one generation embedded as the \(\mathbb C^5\)-leg's contribution. **Kummer-cover deck groups at Z/30:** color \(\mathbb Z/3\) and chirality \(\mathbb Z/2\) appear at gauge rungs \(m=10\) and \(m=15\) respectively (not at Born \(m=2\) or cubic \(m=3\) as at Z/6); SM gauge-center \(\mathbb Z/6=\mathbb Z/3\times\mathbb Z/2\) appears at the **quintic** gauge rung \(m=5\) on Z/30 — the structural signature of "SM-content embedded in Z/30 at a specific (non-Born/cubic) gauge rung." **Interpretation: Z/30 is the GUT-scale row of the framework.** The Z/6 ↔ Z/30 transition is the framework's structural shadow of the SM ↔ GUT transition; SU(5) emerges as a third gauge factor at GUT scale; hypercharge unit refines from \(1/6\) to \(1/30\). **Falsified by Z/30:** "primes in the row = generations" (\(F_{30}\) dim 55, not 45 of 3 generations); "SM lives at Z/30" (SU(5) gauge factor not observed at SM scale); "naive extension to Z/210" (would predict SU(7) gauge factor, no evidence at any scale). **Confirmed by Z/30 (cross-validating Z/6):** \(\sin^2\theta_W^{\text{tree}}=3/8\) is stable; the \(\Lambda^2 E\oplus E^*\) construction is scale-invariant; hypercharge \(Y=\tfrac{1}{2}P_2-\tfrac{1}{3}P_3\) does not need modification at Z/30 (the new prime-5 contributes 0 to hypercharge). **Firewall preserved:** GUT scale itself, running couplings, threshold corrections, proton decay rate — all dimensionful magnitudes — remain out of scope. (§10.6.7b)

- **JJ. [P, structural; partial computational — added v0.2.5] — The fermion-boson selection rule: spin-statistics skeleton from the three-\(\mathbb Z/2\) alignment at \((N=6, m=3)\).** *The framework's spin-statistics correspondence assembles three different \(\mathbb Z/2\)'s that coincide at the smallest mixed primorial: (F-i) **Hopf-fibration parity** — \(2\pi\) rotation of \(\mathbb{CP}^{N-1}\) lifts to \(-1\) on the spinor (T7 §2.1), the spin \((-1)^{2s}\) half; (F-ii) **Kummer-cover deck-element** \(\mu_6/\mu_3\cong\mathbb Z/2\) at \((N=6, m=3)\), generated by \(\xi: z\mapsto -z\) (T7 Prop 3.7(c); §10.5.4 Face E), the cubic-gauge parity; (F-iii) **tensor-exchange parity** on \(E\otimes E\), \(+1\) on \(\text{Sym}^2 E\), \(-1\) on \(\Lambda^2 E\), the statistics half.* **Calculation:** diagonal deck \(\xi^{\otimes k}=(-1)^k\) on \(E^{\otimes k}\) does not separate \(\Lambda^2 E\) from \(\text{Sym}^2 E\) (both \(+1\)); resolution: fermion-parity acts on the *individual* Hopf-bundle spinor, where Hopf parity and Kummer deck *coincide* as the \(\mathbb Z/2\) flipping a single spinor under "\(2\pi\) rotation seen from the amplitude side." Two-particle exchange picks up \(-1\) for \(\Lambda^2 E\) (Slater-determinant), \(+1\) for \(\text{Sym}^2 E\) — antisymmetric statistics ↔ fermion ↔ spin-\(\tfrac{1}{2}\) ↔ non-trivial Hopf bundle, all aligned. **Bosonic-counterpart computation:** \(\text{Sym}^2 E\) decomposes as \((\mathbf 3,\mathbf 1)_{Y=1}\oplus(\mathbf 2,\mathbf 3)_{Y=1/6}\oplus(\mathbf 1,\mathbf 6)_{Y=-2/3}\), \(\dim 15\), \(\mathrm{Tr}(Y^2)|_{\text{Sym}^2 E}=35/6\); does *not* match SM bosonic content (SM gauge bosons in adjoint \(\text{End}(E)\), Higgs in bimodule). The framework provides the spin-statistics skeleton (\(\Lambda\)=fermion, \(\text{Sym}\)=boson) but the specific SM bosonic identification requires additional spectral-triple construction. **What is derived:** fermions in antisymmetric tensor, spin-\(\tfrac{1}{2}\) via Hopf, three-\(\mathbb Z/2\) alignment at the smallest mixed primorial (structural). **What is *not* derived:** the QFT proof from Lorentz invariance + microcausality, the operator-algebra anticommutation \(\{\psi_a,\psi_b^\dagger\}=\delta_{ab}\), the specific SM bosonic content beyond \(\text{Sym}^2 E\). (§10.6.7a)

- **II. [P, computed — added v0.2.5] — The Weinberg-angle calculation: \(\sin^2\theta_W|_{\text{tree}}=3/8\) and the full SM hypercharge spectrum from finite arithmetic on \(\mathbb Z/6\).** *The framework's first dimensionless numerical prediction matching a peer-reviewed Standard-Model value exactly.* Setup: take the spectral-triple inner Hilbert space \(E=\mathbb C^2\oplus\mathbb C^3\) (the CRT direct-sum at the smallest mixed primorial, distinct from the tensor product \(\mathbb C^2\otimes\mathbb C^3\) of the Bures lift); take the fermion representation \(F=\Lambda^2 E\oplus E^*\) (dimension 15, one SM generation, the Connes–Chamseddine module reproduced under SU(2)×SU(3) decomposition); take the prime-reciprocal hypercharge \(Y=\tfrac{1}{2}P_2-\tfrac{1}{3}P_3\) of Paper 33 (with \(P_2,P_3\) projecting onto the CRT factors of \(E\)). **All five SM hypercharge values reproduced exactly**: \(e_R^c\to +1\), \(Q_L\to +1/6\), \(u_R^c\to -2/3\), \(L\to -1/2\), \(d_R^c\to +1/3\). **Trace calculation:** \(\mathrm{Tr}(Y^2)|_F=10/3\), \(\mathrm{Tr}(T_{SU(2)}^2)|_F=\mathrm{Tr}(T_{SU(3)}^2)|_F=2\). **Tree-level Weinberg angle:** \(\sin^2\theta_W|_{\text{tree}}=T_2/(T_2+T_Y)=2/(2+10/3)=6/16=3/8\). **Cross-check:** GUT-normalized \(\hat Y=\sqrt{3/5}\,Y\) gives \(\mathrm{Tr}(\hat Y^2)=2\), equalizing all three generator-trace-squared values on \(F\) — the SU(5) consistency condition holds. **Interpretation:** under the embedding \(SU(2)\times SU(3)\hookrightarrow SU(5)\) with \(E=\mathbf 5_{SU(5)}\), \(\Lambda^2 E\oplus E^*=\mathbf{10}\oplus\bar{\mathbf 5}\) is the SU(5) GUT fermion content per generation — but the framework does *not* postulate SU(5); it has \(E=\mathbb C^2\oplus\mathbb C^3\) forced by the CRT split at \(\mathbb Z/6\). **Firewall preserved:** measured \(\sin^2\theta_W(M_Z)\approx 0.231\) requires RG running from GUT to \(M_Z\) which the framework does not provide; \(3/8\) is the *unification-boundary value*, identical to the SU(5) tree prediction; \(\alpha\), \(m_p/m_e\), \(\alpha_s(M_Z)\), \(G\), Planck scale, generation count, and all dimensionful magnitudes remain permanently out of scope. **The four supporting structural predictions** (Hopf factor of 2 = spin-1/2 / Dirac \(g_e=2\); three colors as \(\mathbb Z/3\) Kummer-cover deck at \((N=6, m=2)\); chirality as \(\mathbb Z/2\) deck at \((N=6, m=3)\); the SM gauge-group center \(\mathbb Z/6=\mathbb Z/2\times\mathbb Z/3\) as the Kummer-cover deck-group decomposition across Born and cubic gauge rungs) are recorded in §10.6.2–§10.6.5 at tier [P, structural], inherited from T1/T7. **The five confirmed predictions together constitute the dimensionless skeleton of one Standard-Model generation derived from finite arithmetic on \(\mathbb Z/6\).** (§10.6 / §10.6.1)

- **HH. [A, structural — added v0.2.5; consolidates FF, GG, and the T-series substrate into a named thesis] — The Unification Thesis: the categorical-simplex framework is arithmetic quantum gravity at finite primorial.** *Six load-bearing recognitions of §10.5.2 — (F0) the Bures lift IS the canonical \(\mathbb{CP}^{N-1}\) amplitude bundle (T7 §1); (F1) quantization IS the Kummer cover (T7 §5); (F2) decoherence IS closure of phase / modulus restriction (T7 §4); (F3) gravity localizes to the multiplicative-unit-indexed additive sector \((\mathbb Z/P_k)^\times\) (§2.5.4 / GG); (F4) matter / gauge localizes to the non-unit additive sector (Paper 32 §6); (F5) finite Dirichlet polynomials are the framework's "QG observables" (T8 §5) — compose into the Unification Thesis (§10.5.3): the framework realizes the gravity-matter decoupling problem of perturbative QG on a finite-arithmetic substrate, with explicit dictionary entries.* The discipline rails of §11.1 / §11.2 / §11.4 preserve unchanged — and are *raised* by the naming: the §11.2 firewall on dimensionful constants (no \(G\), no Planck length, no graviton mass, no metric in meters, no time in seconds) is binding because the structural-shape claim has been named. **Three boundaries Paper 32 should now cross (§10.5.6): (B1) name the Unification Thesis; (B2) open the Face E matched-pair (Kummer-cover deck-group \(\mathbb Z/2\) at \(N=6, m=3\) vs Paper 33's external \(\gamma^5\)-chirality); (B3) name "arithmetic quantum gravity at finite primorial" as the framework's structural-shape claim.** One boundary the framework should NOT cross: no face promotes to a physical claim about spacetime, gravitons, or physical QG. **Five faces (§10.5.4), not four:** A (signature + weak isospin + \(c\)) + B (color) + C (\(i\) + \(\hbar\)) + D (hypercharge \(\mathfrak u(1)_Y\)) + **E (Kummer-cover deck-group \(\mathbb Z/2\), new)**, with the K/L/joint-on-disjoint matched-pair on E ↔ Paper 33's external chirality pre-claimed. **Updates the convergent papers (33, 41, 44, 46, 47, 48, 49) with T-series-substrate language at §10.5.5; no new claims by Paper 32 on those papers, only the substrate's reading of their existing content.** Tier: [A] structural — no part of HH is asserted at [P] independently; HH consolidates pre-existing [P] claims (Paper 32 §4, §5, §6 + Paper 47 audit δ + T7 §1/§5 + Paper 22 §7 cubic) into one thesis. (§10.5)

