## Appendix F: Figure 1 — Instrumented-Run Specification (pre-registered)

Figure 1 is the single panel that must validate three claims at once: the
time-translation closure certificate (§6.4), the arithmetic localization of the
gravity-adjacent residual (Theorem 6.2, §13.1), and the Paper 22 positivity
identification (Theorem 7.1, §13.3). It is one run, post-processed three ways.
This appendix is pre-registered in the sense of Paper 28 §15.10: the pass/fail
inequalities below are fixed *before* execution; a result is reportable only if
the controls pass and the registered thresholds are met without retuning.

### F.1 Substrate: the integrator and coordinates

Integrate the Nambu–Fisher flow on \(\Delta_6^\circ\) with the Paper 14
5-dimensional structure-preserving (discrete-gradient / Nambu-midpoint) scheme,
which preserves the \(Q-2=4\) macro-Hamiltonians \(C_1,\dots,C_4\) and the
Fisher volume \(\Omega_6^F\) to machine precision; the cubic force is
\(\ddot\eta=K^{CH}(v,v)\) (Papers 13, 17). Work in the character basis with the
real packet coordinates of §6.1:
\[
u_{A_2}\in\mathbb{R}\ (\chi_3),\qquad
u_{A_3}=(a_3,b_3)\ (\mathrm{Re},\mathrm{Im}\ \widehat\eta_2),\qquad
u_{M}=(a_M,b_M)\ (\mathrm{Re},\mathrm{Im}\ \widehat\eta_1),
\]
total real dimension \(1+2+2=5\). \(\Pi_\tau\) is the linear map zeroing
\(u_M\).

### F.2 Floor control (defines every "zero")

Before any projection, record the bare invariant drift over the full horizon:
\[
\epsilon_{\mathrm{floor}}
:=\max\Big(\textstyle\max_i\sup_t|C_i(t)-C_i(0)|,\ \sup_t|\mathrm{vol}(t)-\mathrm{vol}(0)|\Big).
\]
All "vanishes" claims below mean \(\le 5\,\epsilon_{\mathrm{floor}}\). If
\(\epsilon_{\mathrm{floor}}\) is not at integrator machine floor the run is void
(the scheme is not the Paper 14 exact integrator).

### F.3 Horizon and ensemble

Horizon \(=\) at least \(20\) Poincaré recurrence times of the regular leaf
(Paper 19), so that boundedness and stability are tested under *horizon
extension*, not merely short time. Ensemble: \(N\ge64\) random initial
conditions on a fixed regular leaf, plus the two mandatory controls of F.7.

### F.4 The three instrumented observables (panels a–c)

**(a) Closure-certificate observable.** Compute the full Noether energy
\(\mathcal E_3(t)\) and the \(\Pi_\tau\)-projected energy
\(\mathcal E_3^{\Pi_\tau}(t)=\tfrac12 g(\dot\eta_A,\dot\eta_A)
+\tfrac13 T_{A_3}(h_A,\dot\eta_A,\dot\eta_A)\), \(\eta_A=\Pi_\tau\eta\). The
defect is \(\Delta(t)=\tfrac{d}{dt}\mathcal E_3^{\Pi_\tau}\). Spectrally
decompose \(\Delta\) into packet content and report the localization fraction
\[
L(t)=\frac{\|\Delta(t)\|_{M}}{\|\Delta(t)\|_{\mathrm{total}}}.
\]
*Registered prediction:* \(\mathcal E_3\) flat at floor (control on faithfulness);
\(\mathcal E_3^{\Pi_\tau}\) **not** conserved; and \(\overline{L}\ge 1-10^{-3}\)
with \(\|\Delta\|_{A_2},\|\Delta\|_{A_3}\le 5\,\epsilon_{\mathrm{floor}}\).

**(b) Residual / boundedness observable.** Per-packet residual norms
\(\|R^{\Pi_\tau}\|_{A_2},\|\cdot\|_{A_3},\|\cdot\|_{M}\) vs time, overlaid with
the §6.4 \(\mathsf B\)-slot envelope
\(\mathcal B(t)=\tfrac13\|T|_M\|\,\|h_M(t)\|\,\|\dot\eta(t)\|^2\).
*Registered prediction:* \(\|R\|_{A_2},\|R\|_{A_3}\le 5\,\epsilon_{\mathrm{floor}}\);
\(\|R\|_{M}>0\), quasi-periodic (not monotone-growing — Paper 19 recurrence),
and \(\|R\|_{M}(t)\le\mathcal B(t)\) for all \(t\) on the full horizon.

**(c) Positivity / Paper 22 hinge.** The conductor-6 Noether form
\(\mathcal Q_6(t)\) (the cubic-order instance of the primorial Noether–Weil
form, Theorem 7.1); plot \(\lambda_{\min}\!\big(\mathcal Q_6(t)\big)\).
*Registered prediction:* \(\lambda_{\min}\ge-5\,\epsilon_{\mathrm{floor}}\) for
all \(t\) on every row of F.5. A single genuine negative excursion
simultaneously falsifies the §6.4 \(\mathsf S\)-slot and flags a Paper 22
positivity stress point — this single curve is the triple-validation hinge.

### F.5 Depth audit overlay (panel d, settles §13.1 / [A] item 8)

Re-run F.4 on the prime-power deepenings, embedding the squarefree
conductor-6 support via the natural marginalization
\(\Delta_{12}\!\to\!\Delta_6\), \(\Delta_{18}\!\to\!\Delta_6\) (pushforward of
the quotient maps \(\mathbb{Z}/12\!\to\!\mathbb{Z}/6\),
\(\mathbb{Z}/18\!\to\!\mathbb{Z}/6\)):

- \(R=\mathbb{Z}/12\mathbb{Z}=\mathbb{Z}/4\times\mathbb{Z}/3\): deepens the
  \(2\)-part; the new prime-power axis is **conductor 4**.
- \(R=\mathbb{Z}/18\mathbb{Z}=\mathbb{Z}/2\times\mathbb{Z}/9\): deepens the
  \(3\)-part; the new prime-power axis is **conductor 9**.

Report the depth-leakage ratio
\[
\rho_{\mathrm{depth}}(t)=\frac{\|R^{\Pi_\tau}(t)\|_{\text{new prime-power axis}}}
{\|R^{\Pi_\tau}(t)\|_{\text{conductor }6}}.
\]
*Registered prediction (pass):* \(\rho_{\mathrm{depth}}\le 5\,\epsilon_{\mathrm{floor}}\)
on the full horizon for both rows — prime-power depth opens **no** new
independent cubic carry axis (confirms Paper 17 §5's structural promotion and
the [A] \(\mathsf B/\mathsf S\) slots). *Fail:* a sustained
\(\rho_{\mathrm{depth}}\) on conductor 4 or 9 above floor — depth is a new
cubic axis; time-translation closure on the row is refuted and a Paper 22
stress point is flagged.

### F.6 Souriau-cocycle read-out (panel d inset, settles §13.3 / [A] item P)

From the *same* trajectories, compute the time-translation moment-map
non-equivariance defect under \(\Pi_\tau\) as the finite Souriau 2-cocycle
\(\theta(\Pi_\tau)\) valued in the dual macro-Hamiltonian algebra
(Barbaresco/Marle construction), and its class \([\theta]\in H^2\) as the
obstruction to an equivariant section. Report \(|[\theta]|\) and its
conductor-6 support fraction \(\sigma_6=\|\theta\|_{M}/\|\theta\|_{\mathrm{total}}\).
*Registered prediction:* \([\theta]\neq0\) (a genuine Noether anomaly exists)
**and** \(\sigma_6\ge 1-10^{-3}\) (it is the conductor-6 class). \([\theta]=0\)
refutes Remark 5.2; \(\sigma_6\) materially below 1 contradicts Lemma 6.1
(falsifier F1).

### F.7 Mandatory controls

- **Null (negative) control.** Initialize with \(u_M(0)=0\). By Corollary 6.1d
  only \(\{2,2,2\},\{4,4,4\}\) survive; registered prediction
  \(\Delta\equiv0\), \(\|R\|_{M}\equiv0\), \([\theta]=0\) to floor. A nonzero
  defect here means the integrator leaks \(M\)-content and the **entire run is
  void** — this is the indispensable artifact check.
- **Planted (positive) control.** Initialize \(u_M(0)=\delta\,\hat e\) for a
  sweep of \(\delta\). Registered prediction: leading-order
  \(\|\Delta\|\propto\delta\) and \(|[\theta]|\propto\delta\) (the
  \(\{1,2,3\},\{1,1,4\}\) cross channels), confirming calibrated sensitivity,
  not noise.
- **Faithfulness control.** Panel (a)'s flat \(\mathcal E_3\) is itself the
  control that the unprojected dynamics conserve the Noether energy.

### F.8 Panel layout

A 2×2 figure: **(a)** \(\mathcal E_3\) (flat) vs \(\mathcal E_3^{\Pi_\tau}\)
(drifting) with a spectral inset showing all drift weight on conductor-6
(\(\overline L\to1\)); **(b)** the three per-packet \(\|R^{\Pi_\tau}\|\) curves
with the \(\mathcal B(t)\) envelope and the null-control flatline overlaid;
**(c)** \(\lambda_{\min}(\mathcal Q_6)\) vs time for
\(\mathbb{Z}/6,\mathbb{Z}/12,\mathbb{Z}/18\) with the zero line drawn — the
positivity/RH hinge; **(d)** \(\rho_{\mathrm{depth}}\) for conductor-4 and
conductor-9 (predicted flat at floor) with an inset bar for \(|[\theta]|\) and
its conductor-6 support fraction \(\sigma_6\).

### F.9 The single pre-registered verdict

The figure **passes** iff, with no retuning: floor control valid; null control
flat; planted control scales linearly; \(\overline L\ge1-10^{-3}\);
\(\|R\|_{M}\le\mathcal B\) on the full horizon; \(\lambda_{\min}(\mathcal Q_6)
\ge-5\epsilon_{\mathrm{floor}}\) on all three rows;
\(\rho_{\mathrm{depth}}\le5\epsilon_{\mathrm{floor}}\); and
\([\theta]\neq0\) with \(\sigma_6\ge1-10^{-3}\). Passing simultaneously
discharges the §6.4 certificate \(\mathsf B/\mathsf S\) slots, [A] item 8
(depth), [A] item P (cocycle), and Theorem 7.1's positivity tie-in. Any single
registered inequality failing is reported as such — a clean negative is a
result (it localizes which of the certificate, the depth promotion, or the
positivity identification breaks), per the Paper 31 §13 guardrail philosophy.

