## Appendix R: Reproducibility — Lemma 6.1 machine verification

Lemma 6.1a/6.1/6.1d are parameter-free and were independently verified by
direct computation, included here for reproducibility (deterministic; no seeds,
no tolerances beyond floating-point):

1. Over all \(216\) ordered triples \((k,l,m)\in\{0,\dots,5\}^3\), the bare sum
   \(36\sum_{a=0}^{5}\omega^{(k+l+m)a}\) equals \(216\) when
   \(k+l+m\equiv0\pmod6\) and \(0\) otherwise, with **zero** violations —
   confirming \(T_{klm}=216\cdot\mathbb{1}[k{+}l{+}m\equiv0\bmod6]\)
   (Lemma 6.1a).
2. Exhaustive enumeration of unordered multisets from \(\{1,\dots,5\}\) with
   sum \(\equiv0\pmod6\) returns **exactly six**:
   \(\{2,2,2\},\{4,4,4\}\) (signature \(A_3^3\)),
   \(\{1,1,4\},\{2,5,5\}\) (\(M,M,A_3\)),
   \(\{1,2,3\},\{3,4,5\}\) (\(M,A_3,A_2\)) — reproducing the §6.2 table
   (Lemma 6.1).
3. The \(\Pi_\tau\)-survivor set (no \(M\)-leg) is **exactly**
   \(\{(2,2,2),(4,4,4)\}\); \(\{3,3,3\}\) has sum \(9\not\equiv0\) and
   \(\{3,3,0\}\) is gauge-killed — confirming \(A_2\) cubic isolation
   (Corollary 6.1d).

This appendix is to be shipped as a standalone script with the 0.3 submission
so any referee reproduces the selection lemma in seconds.
